{"parentUuid":"4a5aa1fd-3610-4079-b7e3-17e318ccbd67","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01X7XtKFgo3MrFPP4wuQkb2j","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's my PR #1009 evaluation — then I'll pivot to `/superpowers:brainstorming` for your two improvement ideas.\n\n## PR #1009 — review pass\n\n**Scope**: +1530/-162 across 16 files on top of PR #993 (`feat/entire-review`). Net changes:\n1. `Review` settings shape: `map[string][]string` → `map[string]ReviewConfig{Skills, Prompt}` — unlocks the custom-prompt UX you called out.\n2. `--track-only` removed; replaced with `entire review attach` + `entire attach --review`.\n3. `--agent NAME` flag for picking among configured agents.\n4. Hooks-installed gate: aborts if the selected agent's hooks aren't installed.\n5. Marker adoption scoping upgraded from `(worktree)` to `(worktree, agent, starting-SHA)`.\n6. `ReviewPrompt` field persisted end-to-end (session state + both v1/v2 committed metadata).\n\n### Strengths\n\n- **Silent-failure hunting is real this time.** The `--agent mismatch` error lists alternatives (`review.go:691`), the hooks gate errors with the exact `entire configure` command to run (`review.go:625`), and the non-launchable-agent path rearranges the cleanup defer *after* `LauncherFor` so a cursor fallback doesn't silently wipe its own marker (`review.go:633-643`). The regression test `TestRunReview_NonLaunchableAgentPreservesMarker` locks that in.\n- **Marker scoping thinks through \"what if multiple sessions race.\"** Worktree match + agent match + SHA freshness, each with a comment explaining why that specific mismatch is left-in-place vs. cleared. The SHA-stale case is rightly cleared (no future session will match), while wrong-agent is left in place (correct agent may still arrive). This is the kind of distinction most PRs gloss over.\n- **`resolveReviewSkills` for attach refuses to silently pull from config.** Comment: \"Silently attaching configured skills would misrepresent the session as having run skills it may not have.\" That's a load-bearing design call — the review record is a factual claim, and the author picks ground-truth over ergonomics.\n- **`mergePickerResults` pins a data-loss bug with a test.** External/uncurated entries the picker can't surface survive `--edit`; previously they'd silently disappear.\n- **Integration tests cover the three hardest cases.** Full adoption → condensation loop, wrong-agent leaves marker, stale SHA clears it.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- The marker adoption logic is a **three-key filter** (worktree, agent, SHA) but each key has *different* semantics on mismatch: worktree/agent leave the marker for a later legitimate claim; SHA clears it because no future session could legitimately match. Encoding \"leave vs. clear\" per-dimension is more nuanced than a typical gate and worth preserving as a principle if more dimensions appear later.\n- `runAttachSurfaceReviewErrors` is an interesting pattern — a wrapper that re-routes error formatting based on `opts.Review`. It's a small leak of surface concerns into the business function, but the alternative (threading a `cobra.Command` into `runAttach` just for `SilenceUsage`) is worse.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\n### Issues found\n\n**🔴 Blocking — backward-compat break in settings (both bots flagged; I confirmed).**\n`EntireSettings.Review` type changed from `map[string][]string` to `map[string]ReviewConfig` with no `UnmarshalJSON` migration. `loadFromFile` uses `json.Decoder` with `DisallowUnknownFields` (and Go's default type-strict unmarshalling). A file with the old shape `{\"review\": {\"claude-code\": [\"/skill\"]}}` fails to decode — and because `settings.Load()` is called by **every** CLI command (lifecycle hooks, `entire enable`, etc.), the breakage is repo-wide, not scoped to `entire review`.\n\nSaving grace: PR #993 is `OPEN` (unmerged), so no shipped release has the old shape. Risk:\n- Anyone who tested `feat/entire-review` locally and persisted an old-shape config.\n- If 993 merges first and 1009 later, any user who runs `entire review --edit` in between will persist old-shape settings and break on the next upgrade.\n\n**Fix options** (pick one):\n- (a) Land 993+1009 as a single squash/merge so no version ever ships the array shape.\n- (b) Add `UnmarshalJSON` on `ReviewConfig` that accepts `[]string` → `{Skills: x}` or object → struct. Safer long-term.\n\n**🟡 Non-blocking — `confirmFirstRunSetup` swallows terminal errors** (Copilot flagged).\n`review.go:268` treats any `form.Run()` error as \"user cancelled\" and returns `false`. In headless/CI or broken-TTY environments, the command exits 0 with no review run and no diagnostic. Changing signature to `(bool, error)` preserves real failures.\n\n**🟡 Low — stale doc comment** (Cursor flagged). `attach_test.go:838-846` has a leftover comment block describing the *opposite* of the current test behavior. 30-second cleanup.\n\n**🟡 Minor — `confirmFirstRunSetup` is also not covered by a test**, and the non-launchable-agent path has only the \"marker persists\" assertion — the scoped prompt message isn't validated in detail. Nitpick-tier.\n\n**🟢 Nice-to-have — `existing[name].Skills` indirections in picker pre-fill** (`review.go:339-340`) work correctly but read a bit thick. Could extract `savedSkillsSet(cfg ReviewConfig)` if you want. Skip if not bothering.\n\n### Verdict\n\n**Approve conditionally on the settings backward-compat fix.** The rest is strong — the error messaging, marker scoping, and test coverage are all material improvements over 993. Easier to ship if it lands atomically with 993.\n\n---"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":44,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1348,"cache_read_input_tokens":106527,"output_tokens":2724,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"stand