{"parentUuid":"bfd02016-a058-49d4-8fed-fc11c9671bc7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01AtADVwVwUwHTt6npTCV7ro","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Codex research complete. Only one review-adjacent built-in exists: **`/review`** (\"review my current changes and find issues\"). Codex does have a plugin/skill system (`/plugins`, `/skills` are built-ins too) — so the discovery path applies to Codex as well.\n\n## Grounded curated shortlists\n\n| Agent | Built-in review-adjacent commands |\n|---|---|\n| **Claude Code** | `/review`, `/security-review`, `/simplify` |\n| **Codex** | `/review` |\n| **Gemini CLI** | (not curated today; skip unless you want to research it) |\n\nPlus discovery for each: scan plugin skill directories on disk for names/descriptions matching review-adjacent keywords.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nReframing from \"curated vs. vetted\" to **\"built-in vs. plugin-installed\"** exposes a much cleaner guarantee: anything in the curated shortlist is literally impossible to miss (it ships with the agent binary), so the silent-failure-on-launch vector *for those commands* goes away entirely. Silent failure only re-enters the picture if the user edits `settings.json` by hand and names something that isn't installed — which we can catch with one runtime re-check before spawn.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\nNow I have enough to propose the design. Two still-open inputs from you before I draft it:\n\n- **Q4 (per-agent vs unified picker layout)** — still open. My lean: per-agent for Phase 1.\n- **Q5 (new, one follow-up from the research):** Codex's curated list is just `/review`. That's a very short default. Three ways to handle:\n  - **A.** Leave it at 1. Users who want more edit `settings.json` or install plugins for the discovery path to surface them.\n  - **B.** Curate a few Codex plugin commands too (e.g. `/codex:adversarial-review`), but 