{"parentUuid":"e837b277-5f02-4bb9-bebe-a789cee2b356","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01KVmvtF4p1kKLSBG6MLMbbz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good — Q4 locked (per-agent). And you're right, 1009 didn't change picker shape; today it iterates configured agents in sequence (`review.go:244`) which reads as one unified flow but is actually per-agent under the hood. Fine as-is.\n\nQ5 opens up a meaningful new direction. Let me split it into two decisions because they're different:\n\n**Q5a — install pointer vs install-on-demand.**\n\nThe moment we handle Gemini (no built-in review skill at all) and Codex (only `/review`), we need *something* to fill the picker. Two ways:\n\n- **Passive (install pointer).** When built-ins ≡ empty-ish and discovery finds nothing, picker shows a non-interactive hint line: \"No review skills detected for gemini. Install with `gemini extensions install <url>` and re-run `entire review --edit`.\" User exits, runs the command, retries. Zero per-agent install plumbing on our side.\n- **Active (install-on-demand).** Picker offers a menu: `[ ] Install gemini-review-tool now`. If selected, we shell out to the agent's own install command, then refresh discovery, then proceed. Needs a per-agent \"recommended install\" registry (tiny — one entry per agent) plus logic to run and verify the install succeeded.\n\n**My lean: passive first.** Active is a smooth UX win but it creates a surface area (per-agent install command, failure modes, \"the install printed an error, what do we do?\") that's easy to regress. Ship passive; if users hit it often enough to complain, promote to active in a follow-up.\n\n**Q5b — gemini scope.** Do you want gemini included in this Phase 1 spec (new curated entry = empty built-ins + install pointer to the public Gemini review tool), or left out for now and handled separately?\n\nMy lean: **include it**. If we're redesigning the picker to handle \"thin built-ins + install hint,\" gemini is the cleanest forcing function. Leaving it out means the design is validated only against Claude (rich) and Codex (one), and we'll find out it doesn't quite fit gemini when we add it later.\n\nOne short answer on 5a+5b and I'll draft the design."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1637,"cache_read_input_tokens":156358,"output_tokens":712,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1637,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":712,"cache_read_input_tokens":156358,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1637,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1637},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaKMCsyaXJ3X3CHwoXSve","type":"assistant","uuid":"185f2b73-5696-4b03-8870-8e540dd4c1ff","timestamp":"2026-04-22T19:19:01.765Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-review","sessionId":"32ff705a-db92-4346-a9c8-70b631ba581d","version":"2.1.117","gitBranch":"feat/entire-review"}
