{"parentUuid":"8c9a2604-4b38-4662-8acb-bd8b56bbc31b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011WHudPQgHEu4c6vjxkRQUc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Locked. Full picture: **built-ins (curated) + disk discovery + install pointer** per agent. Let me walk through the design in three passes and confirm after each.\n\n## Section 1 of 3 — Architecture & data model\n\n### Three sources of skills, composed per agent\n\nEvery agent's skill list in the picker is `builtins ++ discovered ++ maybeInstallHint`, where each source knows how to answer one question:\n\n| Source | What it answers | Per-agent authority |\n|---|---|---|\n| **`curatedBuiltins`** (Go map) | \"What ships with this agent binary?\" | hardcoded in code |\n| **`discoverSkills(agent)`** (new adapter) | \"What review-adjacent plugin skills are installed on disk right now?\" | per-agent `SkillDiscoverer` interface |\n| **`installHint`** (Go map) | \"If the above two are empty, what should I tell the user to install?\" | hardcoded in code |\n\n### Data shapes\n\n```go\ntype curatedSkill struct {\n    Name string // \"/review\"\n    Desc string // \"Review changes and find issues\"\n}\n\ntype SkillDiscoverer interface {\n    // DiscoverReviewSkills walks the agent's on-disk plugin/skill store and\n    // returns anything whose name or description matches review-adjacent\n    // keywords. Safe to call on fresh installs (returns nil, no error).\n    DiscoverReviewSkills(ctx context.Context) ([]curatedSkill, error)\n}\n\ntype installHint struct {\n    // Human-readable line shown when builtins+discovered are both empty\n    // OR as a footer even when some skills exist.\n    Message string   // \"Install `pr-review-toolkit` with `claude plugin install entireio/pr-review-toolkit`\"\n    Keywords []string // used only for telemetry/debug, not display\n}\n\n// Registry data (initial values):\nvar curatedBuiltins = map[string][]curatedSkill{\n    \"claude-code\": {\n        {\"/review\",          \"Review changes and find issues\"},\n        {\"/security-review\", \"Scan git diff for security issues\"},\n        {\"/simplify\",        \"Review recent changes for code quality\"},\n    },\n    \"codex\":        {{\"/review\", \"Review current changes and find issues\"}},\n    \"gemini-cli\":   {}, // no built-in review command\n}\n\nvar installHints = map[string]installHint{\n    \"claude-code\": {Message: \"More review skills: install `pr-review-toolkit` via `claude plugin install …`\"},\n    \"codex\":       {Message: \"More review skills: install `codex-review-pack` via `codex plugins add …`\"},\n    \"gemini-cli\":  {Message: \"Install `gemini-code-review` with `gemini extensions install <url>`\"},\n}\n```\n\nAgents implement `SkillDiscoverer` as an optional capability interface (next to the existing `HookSupport`, `Launcher`). Agents that don't implement it get an empty discovery result — same fallback as \"no skills found.\"\n\n### What changes in the picker output\n\nThe picker's final output is still a `settings.ReviewConfig{Skills, Prompt}` per agent (no settings shape change from 1009). The new machinery is entirely in how we *build the options list shown to the user*. Settings on disk stay identical to 1009's shape — we're not breaking 1009's backward-compat debt any further.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nModeling `SkillDiscoverer` as a capability interface (like `Launcher` and `HookSupport` today, `agent.go:258-270`) keeps per-agent install-path knowledge local to each agent package. `review.go` only knows about the interface, never about `~/.claude/plugins` or `~/.codex/` paths. If Factory AI Droid or Copilot ever want in, they implement the interface and register; no changes in review code.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\n---\n\nDoes section 1 (data model + where the new plumbing lives) look right before I move into the discovery algorithm specifics (how each agent's `DiscoverReviewSkills` actually scans disk and what \"review-adjacent\" match rule to use)?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2372,"cache_read_input_tokens":158731,"output_tokens":1367,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2372,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1367,"cache_read_input_tokens":158731,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2372,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2372},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaKMKviERLzuskDcxN8S2","type":"assistant","uuid":"0cba0462-162d-4645-92c7-627deb9dc0ea","timestamp":"2026-04-22T19:20:44.296Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-review","sessionId":"32ff705a-db92-4346-a9c8-70b631ba581d","version":"2.1.117","gitBranch":"feat/entire-review"}
