{"parentUuid":"98e5f367-e1dc-4947-b4d0-d9c1ff1a5094","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01VkQzCmEVSenP9pLktHtU6W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Section 3 of 3 — Picker flow, runtime re-verification, edge cases, testing\n\n### End-to-end picker flow (no behavior change below the picker)\n\n```\nentire review (first-run, no config)\n  │\n  ├─ confirmFirstRunSetup (1009) ────── user confirms? ── no ──► exit 0\n  │                                         │\n  │                                        yes\n  ├─ runReviewConfigPicker\n  │     │\n  │     ├─ eligible agents := installed_and_hooked ∩ (builtins ∪ installHints)\n  │     │     (NEW: gemini becomes eligible because it has an installHint)\n  │     │\n  │     └─ for agent in alphabetical(eligible):\n  │           builtins  := curatedBuiltins[agent]\n  │           disc      := agent.DiscoverReviewSkills(ctx)      ← empty if no discoverer\n  │           hints     := installHints[agent] minus suppressed-by(disc)\n  │           render huh.NewGroup(\n  │               builtinField(builtins | noteIfEmpty),\n  │               discoveredField(disc | noteIfEmpty),\n  │               installHintNotes(hints),                      ← omit section if hints empty\n  │               customPromptText,\n  │           )\n  │           cfg := ReviewConfig{\n  │               Skills: dedupe(builtinPicks ++ discoveredPicks),\n  │               Prompt: strings.TrimSpace(promptText),\n  │           }\n  │\n  ├─ mergePickerResults (1009, unchanged)\n  └─ save to settings.json\n```\n\nEverything below that (`selectReviewAgent`, hooks-installed gate, marker write, launcher spawn) is unchanged from 1009 **except** the new re-verification step below.\n\n### Runtime re-verification at spawn\n\nNew guard, executed between `selectReviewAgent` and marker write in `runReview`:\n\n```go\nfunc verifyConfiguredSkillsInstalled(ctx context.Context, ag agent.Agent, cfg settings.ReviewConfig) error {\n    if len(cfg.Skills) == 0 { return nil } // prompt-only config — nothing to verify\n\n    builtins := curatedBuiltinNames(ag.Name())\n    var discoveredNames map[string]struct{}\n    if d, ok := ag.(agent.SkillDiscoverer); ok {\n        skills, _ := d.DiscoverReviewSkills(ctx)\n        discoveredNames = namesOf(skills)\n    }\n\n    var missing []string\n    for _, s := range cfg.Skills {\n        if _, ok := builtins[s]; ok           { continue }\n        if _, ok := discoveredNames[s]; ok    { continue }\n        missing = append(missing, s)\n    }\n    if len(missing) == 0 { return nil }\n    return fmt.Errorf(\n        \"configured review skill(s) not installed: %s\\n\"+\n        \"run `entire review --edit` to reconfigure, or install the plugin and retry\",\n        strings.Join(missing, \", \"),\n    )\n}\n```\n\nTriggered by the *same* error-surfacing pattern as the hooks-installed gate in 1009:\n\n```go\nif err := verifyConfiguredSkillsInstalled(ctx, ag, cfg); err != nil {\n    cmd.SilenceUsage = true\n    fmt.Fprintln(cmd.ErrOrStderr(), err.Error())\n    return NewSilentError(err)\n}\n```\n\nThis is the spawn-time backstop for the case the picker can't prevent: user hand-edits `settings.json` and types `/foo:bar` that isn't installed. Without this, `entire review` would spawn, send the composed prompt, and the agent would reply \"I don't have that skill\" — the silent-failure shape we're explicitly engineering out.\n\n### Edge cases (enumerated with intended behavior)\n\n| Scenario | Behavior |\n|---|---|\n| No built-ins, no discovered, install hint present (Gemini fresh) | Picker shows two empty-state notes + hint + prompt textarea. User types a Prompt → saves prompt-only config. User leaves blank → final `mergePickerResults` empty-check fires (1009). |\n| No built-ins, discovered exists (hypothetical future agent) | Built-in section shows \"(none)\" note; discovered section populated. Works. |\n| Built-ins exist, discovery fails with I/O error | Built-in section populated; discovered section shows \"(none)\" note (error logged at Debug). Picker still usable. |\n| Discovery finds 50+ skills | All rendered. huh scrolls. User scrolls. Acceptable — this is rare. |\n| User picks nothing but types prompt | `ReviewConfig{Skills: nil, Prompt: \"…\"}` saved. `composeReviewPrompt` returns Prompt verbatim at spawn (1009 behavior, unchanged). |\n| User picks a discovered skill, then uninstalls the plugin before running `entire review` | Spawn-time re-verification fails. Clear error with remediation, non-zero exit. |\n| User's `settings.json` references a skill name outside both built-ins and discovered | Same re-verification failure. |\n| 1009's backward-compat break with old `map[string][]string` shape | **Out of scope for this spec.** Assumed resolved in 1009 (either `UnmarshalJSON` migration or atomic land with 993). Noted as a dependency. |\n\n### Testing strategy\n\n**Unit tests (new or extended):**\n\n- `discoverer_test.go` per agent (start: claudecode). Temp dir fixtures:\n  - Empty plugin dir → nil, nil\n  - Plugin with 1 review skill + 1 non-review skill → 1 result\n  - Malformed SKILL.md → skipped, no error\n  - Permission-denied subdir → skipped, logged\n- `skilldiscovery/match_test.go` — keyword match on name AND description, case-insensitive, every keyword covered\n- `review_test.go` extensions:\n  - `TestInstallHintSuppressedWhenProvidesAnyMatchesDiscovered`\n  - `TestInstallHintShownWhenProvidesAnyEmpty`\n  - `TestPickerRendersEmptyBuiltinsAsNote`\n  - `TestPickerRendersEmptyDiscoveredAsNote`\n  - `TestPickerDedupesBuiltinVsDiscovered`\n  - `TestRunReview_MissingSkillAbortsAtSpawn`\n  - `TestRunReview_PromptOnlyConfigSkipsSkillVerification`\n- Pin the current behavior with a golden test for the composed picker form structure (fields, titles, empty-state notes) — not a full huh render, just the declarative structure\n\n**Integration tests (extend `integration_test/review_test.go`):**\n\n- Fresh Claude Code install, no plugins → picker offers 3 built-ins + install hint; saved config runs without re-verification error\n- Claude Code + `/pr-review-toolkit:review-pr` fixture on disk → picker offers built-ins + discovered; install hint for pr-review-toolkit suppressed (because it provides `/pr-review-toolkit:review-pr`); install hint for other packages shown\n- Missing-at-spawn: pre-write `settings.json` with `/nonexistent:skill`, run `entire review`, assert stderr match + exit code + marker NOT written\n\n**No E2E tests.** All changes are config-time; no real-agent behavior changes. Existing E2E canary (Vogon) continues to cover the spawn→adopt→commit loop.\n\n### Non-goals (explicit, so reviewers don't ask)\n\n- **Install-on-demand / active install flow** — deferred; the passive hint is the Phase 1 answer.\n- **Codex / Gemini discovery implementations** — interface in place, implementations return `nil, nil` until their on-disk layouts are verified against source. Claude Code ships with a real implementation Day 1.\n- **Settings shape change** — no change; we build on 1009's `ReviewConfig` shape.\n- **Multi-agent parallel spawn, ctrl-o panes, aggregated summary** — Phase 2, separate spec.\n\n---\n\nSection 3 complete. That's the full design:\n1. Three-source composition (built-ins + discovery + install hint) with `ProvidesAny` suppression and dedupe.\n2. `SkillDiscoverer` as an optional capability interface, per-agent.\n3. Keyword-matched discovery, Claude Code Day 1, Codex/Gemini stubbed.\n4. Spawn-time re-verification as the silent-failure backstop.\n\nDoes the whole thing cohere, or anything you want to reshape before I write it to `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-22-entire-review-picker-install-awareness-design.md` and kick off the spec review loop?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":169663,"output_tokens":4935,"server_tool_use":{"web_s