{"parentUuid":"7b55001b-5f75-479b-af9b-d343dd5c15d4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01ChBDw6eVr4BPprKBGsLGLr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01D1dsR2UJx3ap6JzJ9r36PZ","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-review/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-22-entire-review-picker-install-awareness-design.md","content":"# `entire review` — install-aware picker (Phase 1)\n\n**Status:** design — awaiting implementation plan\n**Date:** 2026-04-22\n**Author:** Peyton Montei (with Claude Opus 4.7)\n**Base branch:** `feat/entire-review` (PR #993 + #1009 stack)\n\n## Problem\n\nThe picker in `entire review` (PR #993, hardened in PR #1009) offers a hardcoded list of review skills per agent (`cmd/entire/cli/review.go:126`). Nearly every entry in that list — `/pr-review-toolkit:review-pr`, `/pr-review-toolkit:code-reviewer`, `/test-auditor`, `/requesting-code-review`, `/codex:adversarial-review` — requires a plugin install before the agent can resolve it. Users can pick these skills in the picker whether or not they have the plugin installed. When they don't, running `entire review` spawns the agent with a prompt like `Please run /pr-review-toolkit:review-pr`, the agent replies \"I don't have that skill,\" and the session is recorded as a review even though no review ran. Silent failure.\n\nCompounding: Gemini CLI has no built-in review command and no curated entry today, so users with only Gemini installed never see Gemini as a pickable option at all.\n\n## Goals\n\n1. **Eliminate the \"skill not installed\" silent-failure vector.** Users should not be able to configure a review session around skills that aren't present on disk.\n2. **Make discoverability a first-class concern.** Users should see the full set of review-relevant skills actually available to them — built-in and installed plugins alike — and should know where to install more.\n3. **Keep the picker scope per-agent** (Phase 1 is single-agent; multi-agent parallel spawn is Phase 2).\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Install-on-demand / active install flow — passive hints only for Phase 1.\n- Changing the settings.json shape — we build on `settings.ReviewConfig` as introduced in PR #1009.\n- Multi-agent parallel spawn, ctrl-o panes, aggregated cross-agent summary — Phase 2 spec.\n- Full Codex and Gemini CLI discovery implementations — interface is in place Day 1, implementations are stubbed and land in follow-up PRs once their on-disk layouts are verified against source.\n\n## Architecture overview\n\nPer agent, the picker's options list is composed from three sources, rendered in three always-present sections plus a custom-prompt field:\n\n```\n builtins      := curatedBuiltins[agent]                 // hardcoded, guaranteed on disk\n discovered    := agent.DiscoverReviewSkills(ctx)        // scan agent's plugin/skill store\n activeHints   := installHints[agent] − suppressed-by-discovered\n```\n\nFinal picker form (huh group):\n\n1. **Built-in commands** — multi-select of `builtins`, or a note when `builtins` is empty.\n2. **Installed plugin skills** — multi-select of `discovered`, or a note when `discovered` is empty.\n3. **Install more** — `huh.NewNote` lines for each unsuppressed entry in `activeHints`. Section omitted entirely if all hints suppressed (so users who have everything installed never see a nag).\n4. **Additional instructions (optional)** — `huh.NewText` for a custom prompt. Unchanged from PR #1009.\n\nOn picker save, `builtinPicks ++ discoveredPicks` are deduped and stored as `ReviewConfig.Skills`; the textarea content is trimmed and stored as `ReviewConfig.Prompt`. `mergePickerResults` (PR #1009, unchanged) preserves uncurated / external-agent entries the picker couldn't offer.\n\n### Why a capability interface for discovery\n\n`Agent` already uses optional capability interfaces for `Launcher`, `HookSupport`, and others (`cmd/entire/cli/agent/agent.go:258-299`). Adding `SkillDiscoverer` the same way keeps per-agent install-path knowledge local to each agent package. `review.go` never imports `~/.claude/plugins/...` — it asks the agent, \"do you have a discoverer, and if so what's on disk?\"\n\n## Data model\n\nAll new types live either in the agent package (the interface) or in a new `cmd/entire/cli/agent/skilldiscovery/` package (shared helpers + registry data).\n\n```go\n// cmd/entire/cli/agent/agent.go\ntype DiscoveredSkill struct {\n    Name        string // e.g. \"/pr-review-toolkit:review-pr\"\n    Description string // from SKILL.md frontmatter `description:` if available, else \"\"\n    SourcePath  string // absolute path — debug logging only; not shown in picker\n}\n\ntype SkillDiscoverer interface {\n    Agent\n    // DiscoverReviewSkills scans the agent's on-disk plugin/skill store and\n    // returns anything whose name or description matches review-adjacent\n    // keywords. Safe on fresh installs — returns nil, nil for missing dirs.\n    DiscoverReviewSkills(ctx context.Context) ([]DiscoveredSkill, error)\n}\n```\n\n```go\n// cmd/entire/cli/agent/skilldiscovery/registry.go\ntype curatedSkill struct {\n    Name string\n    Desc string\n}\n\ntype installHint struct {\n    Message     string   // rendered as a note line in the picker\n    ProvidesAny []string // if any of these names appear in DiscoveredSkills, hint is suppressed\n}\n\nvar CuratedBuiltins = map[string][]curatedSkill{\n    \"claude-code\": {\n        {\"/review\",          \"Review changes and find issues\"},\n        {\"/security-review\", \"Scan git diff for security issues\"},\n        {\"/simplify\",        \"Review recent changes for code quality\"},\n    },\n    \"codex\":      {{\"/review\", \"Review current changes and find issues\"}},\n    \"gemini-cli\": {}, // no built-in review command\n}\n\nvar InstallHints = map[string][]installHint{\n    \"claude-code\": {\n        {Message: \"Install `pr-review-toolkit` via `claude plugin install entireio/pr-review-toolkit`\",\n         ProvidesAny: []string{\"/pr-review-toolkit:review-pr\", \"/pr-review-toolkit:code-reviewer\", \"/pr-review-toolkit:silent-failure-hunter\"}},\n        {Message: \"Install `test-auditor` via the superpowers plugin\",\n         ProvidesAny: []string{\"/test-auditor\"}},\n    },\n    \"codex\": {\n        {Message: \"Install `codex-review-pack` via `codex plugins add …`\",\n         ProvidesAny: []string{\"/codex:adversarial-review\"}},\n    },\n    \"gemini-cli\": {\n        {Message: \"Install `gemini-code-review` via `gemini extensions install <url>`\",\n         ProvidesAny: nil}, // no known skill name to detect; always show\n    },\n}\n\nvar reviewKeywords = []string{\n    \"review\", \"audit\", \"inspect\", \"critique\",\n    \"assess\", \"security-scan\", \"lint\",\n}\n```\n\n**The exact install commands and `ProvidesAny` lists are pinned by real plugin/marketplace metadata at implementation time.** The shape is what's frozen here.\n\n## Discovery algorithm\n\n### Shared contract\n\n`skilldiscovery.Matches(name, description string) bool` — case-insensitive substring match: returns true if `name` or `description` contains any entry in `reviewKeywords`. Shared across all agent implementations so keyword semantics stay consistent.\n\n### Per-agent scan rules\n\n| Agent | Scan root(s) | Skill entry shape | Name format |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **claude-code** | `~/.claude/plugins/cache/<marketplace>/<plugin>/<version>/skills/<skill>/SKILL.md` + `~/.claude/skills/<skill>/SKILL.md` | one directory per skill; YAML frontmatter | `/<plugin>:<skill>` for plugin skills, `/<skill>` for user skills |\n| **codex** | TBD — verify against `codex-rs/tui/src/...` source for skill/plugin dir layout; current observation is `~/.codex/plugins/<plugin>/` | TBD (SKILL.md or TOML manifest) | `/<plugin>:<skill>` (convention observed in `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/AGENT.md`) |\n| **gemini-cli** | TBD — verify Gemini extensions layout | per Gemini extension manifest | `/<extension-command>` |\n\n**Implementation ordering:** Claude Code discoverer lands Day 1. Codex and Gemini implementations return `nil, nil` until their on-disk layouts are verified from source; the `SkillDiscoverer` interface and registry entries for built-ins and install hints are in place immediately so the picker renders correctly for all three agents.\n\n### Performance\n\nDiscovery runs only inside the picker (first-run or `entire review --edit`). Worst-case scan for a user with 50 plugin skills is ~50 small file reads — well under 100ms on any modern disk. No cache. Simpler is better.\n\n### Graceful failure\n\n`DiscoverReviewSkills` returns `(skills, error)`. All callers treat an error as \"found nothing\" and log at Debug; discovery never blocks the picker.\n\n- Plugin dir doesn't exist (fresh install, no plugins) → `nil, nil`. Not an error.\n- Malformed SKILL.md → skip that skill, log, continue.\n- Permission error on a subdir → skip, log, continue.\n- Home directory inaccessible → `nil, nil`.\n\n## Picker flow\n\n### Eligibility\n\nAn agent appears in the picker if it is:\n\n1. Installed with entire hooks (`GetAgentsWithHooksInstalled`, existing in `review.go:196`), AND\n2. Has a non-empty entry in **either** `CuratedBuiltins` **or** `InstallHints`.\n\nRule (2) is the change: today the filter requires a non-empty `CuratedBuiltins` entry. The new filter is `CuratedBuiltins ∪ InstallHints`, which admits Gemini (empty built-ins but has a hint) without requiring us to curate built-ins we don't actually have.\n\n### Per-agent rendering\n\n```go\nfor _, agent := range alphabetical(eligibleAgents) {\n    builtins    := CuratedBuiltins[agent.Name()]\n    discovered, _ := asSkillDiscovererOrNil(agent).DiscoverReviewSkills(ctx) // nil-safe\n    discoveredSet := namesOf(discovered)\n\n    // Dedupe: if a \"discovered\" skill name matches a built-in, drop the\n    // discovered row (built-in wins, richer description).\n    discovered = filterOut(discovered, func(d DiscoveredSkill) bool {\n        return containsBuiltin(builtins, d.Name)\n    })\n\n    // Filter install hints via ProvidesAny suppression.\n    activeHints := filter(InstallHints[agent.Name()], func(h installHint) bool {\n        for _, name := range h.ProvidesAny {\n            if _, ok := discoveredSet[name]; ok { return false }\n        }\n        return true\n    })\n\n    form := NewAccessibleForm(huh.NewGroup(\n        builtinField(builtins),               // multi-select OR note\n        discoveredField(discovered),          // multi-select OR note\n        installHintNotes(activeHints),        // 0..n huh.Note; section hidden if 0\n        customPromptText(existing.Prompt),    // huh.Text\n    ))\n    form.Run()\n\n    cfg := settings.ReviewConfig{\n        Skills: dedupe(builtinPicks ++ discoveredPicks),\n        Prompt: strings.TrimSpace(promptText),\n    }\n    if !cfg.IsZero() {\n        selected[agent.Name()] = cfg\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Empty-state notes\n\nWhen a section has no options, substitute the multi-select with a `huh.NewNote`:\n\n- Empty `builtins` → note body: `No built-in review commands in <agent>.`\n- Empty `discovered` → note body: `No plugin review skills detected on disk.`\n- Empty `activeHints` → section **omitted entirely** (no note, no heading). We don't want a \"nothing to install\" footer when the user has a rich setup.\n\n## Runtime re-verification\n\nA new guard runs between `selectReviewAgent` and marker write in `runReview`:\n\n```go\nif err := verifyConfiguredSkillsInstalled(ctx, ag, cfg); err != nil {\n    cmd.SilenceUsage = true\n    fmt.Fprintln(cmd.ErrOrStderr(), err.Error())\n    return NewSilentError(err)\n}\n```\n\n```go\nfunc verifyConfiguredSkillsInstalled(ctx context.Context, ag agent.Agent, cfg settings.ReviewConfig) error {\n    if len(cfg.Skills) == 0 {\n        return nil // prompt-only config — nothing to verify\n    }\n    builtins := curatedBuiltinNamesForAgent(ag.Name())\n    var discoveredNames map[string]struct{}\n    if d, ok := ag.(agent.SkillDiscoverer); ok {\n        skills, _ := d.DiscoverReviewSkills(ctx)\n        discoveredNames = namesOf(skills)\n    }\n    var missing []string\n    for _, s := range cfg.Skills {\n        if _, ok := builtins[s]; ok        { continue }\n        if _, ok := discoveredNames[s]; ok { continue }\n        missing = append(missing, s)\n    }\n    if len(missing) == 0 {\n        return nil\n    }\n    return fmt.Errorf(\n        \"configured review skill(s) not installed: %s\\n\"+\n        \"run `entire review --edit` to reconfigure, or install the plugin and retry\",\n        strings.Join(missing, \", \"),\n    )\n}\n```\n\nThis catches the case the picker can't: the user hand-edits `settings.json` and names a skill that isn't on disk, or removes a plugin without updating review config. Without this guard, `entire review` would spawn, compose the prompt, and the agent would respond \"I don't have that skill\" — restoring the silent-failure shape we're engineering out.\n\n## Edge cases\n\n| Scenario | Behavior |\n|---|---|\n| Fresh Gemini install, picker shows 0 built-ins + 0 discovered + 1 hint | User can type a custom prompt alone → prompt-only `ReviewConfig`. If they leave blank, `mergePickerResults` emptiness check fires (PR #1009, unchanged). |\n| Built-ins present, discovery fails with I/O error | Built-ins section normal; discovered section shows `(none)` note. Error logged at Debug. |\n| Discovery finds 50+ skills | All rendered. huh scrolls. No silent truncation. |\n| User picks nothing, types prompt | `{Skills: nil, Prompt: \"…\"}` saved. `composeReviewPrompt` returns Prompt verbatim at spawn (PR #1009, unchanged). |\n| User picks a discovered skill, uninstalls its plugin, runs `entire review` | Runtime re-verification fails. Clear error, remediation, non-zero exit. |\n| `settings.json` references a skill outside both sources | Same re-verification failure. |\n| Multiple install hints for same agent, some suppressed and some not | Unsuppressed hints render; suppressed hints hidden. Section heading shows if ≥1 hint survives. |\n| All install hints suppressed (user has everything) | \"Install more\" section omitted (no heading, no body). |\n\n### Dependency on PR #1009's settings shape compat\n\nPR #1009 changed `EntireSettings.Review` from `map[string][]string` → `map[string]ReviewConfig`. That change has a backward-compat break for any user with the old array-shape persisted (flagged by Cursor Bugbot + Copilot on the PR). **This spec assumes that break is resolved in PR #1009's landing**, either by:\n\n- Adding `UnmarshalJSON` on `ReviewConfig` that accepts both array and object shapes, OR\n- Squash-merging PR #993 and PR #1009 together so no released version ever ships the array shape.\n\nThe Phase 1 spec does not introduce or remediate that concern; it depends on 1009 being clean before landing.\n\n## Testing strategy\n\n### Unit tests\n\nNew file `cmd/entire/cli/agent/skilldiscovery/match_test.go`:\n\n- `TestMatches_NameKeywords` — each entry in `reviewKeywords` matches when appearing in the name.\n- `TestMatches_DescriptionKeywords` — each keyword matches when appearing in the description.\n- `TestMatches_CaseInsensitive`.\n- `TestMatches_NoMatchWhenNeitherFieldContainsKeyword`.\n\nNew file `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/discovery_test.go` (and symmetrical stubs for codex / geminicli):\n\n- Temp dir fixture simulating `~/.claude/plugins/cache/...`:\n  - Empty plugins dir → `nil, nil`.\n  - Plugin with one review-matching skill + one non-matching → returns one result.\n  - Plugin with malformed SKILL.md → skip, log, no error.\n  - Plugin with permission-denied subdir → skip, log, no error.\n  - Plugin with skill whose name matches a built-in → caller dedupes (tested separately).\n\nExtend `cmd/entire/cli/review_test.go`:\n\n- `TestInstallHint_SuppressedWhenProvidesAnyMatchesDiscovered`.\n- `TestInstallHint_ShownWhenProvidesAnyEmpty` (Gemini case).\n- `TestPicker_EligibilityIncludesAgentsWithInstallHintEvenWhenBuiltinsEmpty`.\n- `TestPicker_DedupesBuiltinVsDiscovered` — if discovery returns a name that collides with a built-in, built-in wins and discovered is dropped.\n- `TestRunReview_MissingConfiguredSkillAbortsAtSpawn` — pre-seeded `settings.json` with `/nonexistent:skill`, expects stderr match + non-zero exit + marker NOT written.\n- `TestRunReview_PromptOnlyConfigSkipsSkillVerification` — no skills configured but Prompt set, spawn proceeds.\n\n### Integration tests\n\nExtend `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/review_test.go`:\n\n- `TestReview_FreshClaudeCode_PickerOffersBuiltinsAndHints` — fresh install, no plugin dir, picker-produced `ReviewConfig.Skills` is subset of built-ins, config saves, spawn proceeds.\n- `TestReview_ClaudeCodeWithPlugin_PickerOffersDiscovered` — pre-create `~/.claude/plugins/cache/<fake-market>/<fake-plugin>/...` fixture with a review-matching SKILL.md, picker surfaces it, install hint for that plugin suppressed.\n- `TestReview_MissingSkillAtSpawn_ErrorsCleanly` — pre-write `settings.json` with a non-existent skill, assert stderr wording, exit code, no pending marker on disk.\n\n### E2E\n\nNo new E2E tests. All changes are config-time; no real-agent behavior changes. Existing Vogon canary continues to cover the spawn → adopt → commit loop.\n\n## Follow-ups (Phase 2 and beyond)\n\n- **Multi-agent parallel spawn**, ctrl-o pane UX, aggregated cross-agent summary (Phase 2 spec, separate brainstorm).\n- **Real Codex `SkillDiscoverer`** — pending code path check in `codex-rs` source.\n- **Real Gemini `SkillDiscoverer`** — pending Gemini extensions layout research.\n- **Install-on-demand** — promote passive install hints to an interactive \"install now?\" flow. Deferred because it couples the CLI to per-agent install subprocesses and their failure modes.\n- **Surface `ReviewSkills` + `ReviewPrompt` in `entire explain` output** — already on the PR #993 follow-up list; not in scope for this spec.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1264,"cache_read_input_tokens":180892,"output_tokens":7058,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1264,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":7058,"cache_read_input_tokens":180892,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1264,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1264},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaKWZ4N1cvftqHDFgubr5","type":"assistant","uuid":"dcfeb7c1-9ade-4b49-ab64-b85adc4eb57e","timestamp":"2026-04-22T21:23:11.995Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-review","sessionId":"32ff705a-db92-4346-a9c8-70b631ba581d","version":"2.1.117","gitBranch":"feat/entire-review"}
