{"parentUuid":"fc0cd65e-7fec-4ee7-839f-a6eb9aec079f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_016VRMoBTf6Zyx9YjM8QhCrS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018NPZsyKz7UxSLpWeXR63R7","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-review/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-04-22-entire-review-picker-install.md","content":"# Install-Aware Picker for `entire review` — Phase 1 Implementation Plan\n\n> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (if subagents available) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.\n\n**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-22-entire-review-picker-install-awareness-design.md`\n\n**Goal:** Replace the hardcoded, plugin-dependent curated-skills list in `entire review` with a three-source picker (built-ins + on-disk discovery + install hints) plus a runtime re-verification guard, eliminating the silent-failure vector where users pick uninstalled skills.\n\n**Architecture:** New `SkillDiscoverer` capability interface on `agent.Agent`, plus a new `cmd/entire/cli/agent/skilldiscovery/` package holding the curated registries and keyword match helper. Claude Code gets a real discoverer; Codex and Gemini get stubs returning `(nil, nil)` until their disk layouts are verified. Picker rendering in `review.go` composes three `huh` form sections (with `huh.NewNote` empty-state filler) plus the existing custom-prompt textarea. Runtime guard `verifyConfiguredSkillsInstalled` fires between `selectReviewAgent` and pending-marker write.\n\n**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26.x, Cobra, huh, go-git/v6, `mise`/`golangci-lint`/Vogon canary for CI.\n\n**Branch strategy:** Add commits directly on top of the existing PR #1009 branch (`soph/entire-review-2`) — no new branch. PR #1009 absorbs the picker-install work. Five commits total, one per chunk.\n\n**Commit model:** Per chunk, implement all tasks in order (test → red → impl → green for each), run `mise run check` as the local build gate, then commit the whole chunk as one logical unit. No per-task commits.\n\n---\n\n## Preamble — confirm base branch state\n\n- [ ] **P.1: Verify working branch is `soph/entire-review-2` (PR #1009)**\n\nRun:\n```bash\ngit rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD\n```\nExpected: `soph/entire-review-2`. If it's anything else — and especially if it's `main`, `feat/entire-review`, or a fresh worktree — stop and switch before continuing.\n\n- [ ] **P.2: Verify PR #1009's helpers are present**\n\nRun:\n```bash\ngrep -n \"type ReviewConfig\\|func mergePickerResults\\|func confirmFirstRunSetup\\|func selectReviewAgent\" \\\n  cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go cmd/entire/cli/review.go\n```\nExpected: all four symbols present. If any missing, the working branch is wrong — stop and re-confirm with the user.\n\n- [ ] **P.3: Baseline `mise run check`**\n\nRun: `mise run check`\nExpected: PASS. This baselines the tree so any failures during implementation are *our* changes, not pre-existing.\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 1 — `SkillDiscoverer` interface + `skilldiscovery` package\n\nOne commit at the end of this chunk.\n\n### Files\n\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/agent.go` (add `DiscoveredSkill` type + `SkillDiscoverer` interface near the other capability interfaces around line 258-299)\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/skilldiscovery/match.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/skilldiscovery/match_test.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/skilldiscovery/registry.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/skilldiscovery/registry_test.go`\n\n### Task 1 — Add `SkillDiscoverer` capability interface\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Verify the interface does not yet exist**\n\nRun: `grep -n \"SkillDiscoverer\\b\\|DiscoveredSkill\\b\" cmd/entire/cli/agent/agent.go`\nExpected: zero matches.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Add the type + interface**\n\nInsert the block below into `cmd/entire/cli/agent/agent.go`, immediately after the `Launcher` interface:\n\n```go\n// DiscoveredSkill describes one review-adjacent skill found on disk by a\n// SkillDiscoverer. Name is the agent-native invocation form (e.g. a\n// slash-prefixed command); Description is scraped from on-disk metadata\n// if available; SourcePath is kept for debug logging and is not shown to\n// the user.\ntype DiscoveredSkill struct {\n\tName        string\n\tDescription string\n\tSourcePath  string\n}\n\n// SkillDiscoverer is implemented by agents that can enumerate review-adjacent\n// skills installed locally on disk (e.g. plugin skills under\n// ~/.claude/plugins/...). This powers the \"Installed plugin skills\" section\n// of the `entire review` picker and the runtime verification that configured\n// skills still exist before spawn.\n//\n// Contract:\n//   - Safe to call on fresh installs where no plugin dir exists yet —\n//     return (nil, nil), not an error.\n//   - Malformed individual skill metadata must be skipped with a Debug log,\n//     not propagated as an error.\n//   - A (nil, non-nil) error means \"discovery could not run at all\" (e.g.\n//     home dir inaccessible). Callers may treat all errors as \"found nothing\"\n//     and log at Debug — discovery must never block the picker.\ntype SkillDiscoverer interface {\n\tAgent\n\tDiscoverReviewSkills(ctx context.Context) ([]DiscoveredSkill, error)\n}\n```\n\n`context` is already imported (line 7). No new imports.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Verify package compiles**\n\nRun: `go build ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/...`\nExpected: PASS.\n\n### Task 2 — Keyword match helper\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing tests**\n\nCreate `cmd/entire/cli/agent/skilldiscovery/match_test.go`:\n```go\npackage skilldiscovery_test\n\nimport (\n\t\"testing\"\n\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/skilldiscovery\"\n)\n\nfunc TestMatches_NameKeywords(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\tcases := []string{\"/review\", \"/security-audit\", \"/inspect-pr\", \"/critique\", \"/assess\"}\n\tfor _, name := range cases {\n\t\tname := name\n\t\tt.Run(name, func(t *testing.T) {\n\t\t\tt.Parallel()\n\t\t\tif !skilldiscovery.Matches(name, \"\") {\n\t\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"Matches(%q, \\\"\\\") = false, want true\", name)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t})\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestMatches_DescriptionKeywords(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\tif !skilldiscovery.Matches(\"/unrelated\", \"Find silent failures during code review\") {\n\t\tt.Error(\"description containing 'review' should match\")\n\t}\n\tif !skilldiscovery.Matches(\"/unrelated\", \"Audit test coverage on changed files\") {\n\t\tt.Error(\"description containing 'audit' should match\")\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestMatches_CaseInsensitive(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\tif !skilldiscovery.Matches(\"/REVIEW\", \"\") {\n\t\tt.Error(\"uppercase name keyword should match\")\n\t}\n\tif !skilldiscovery.Matches(\"/run\", \"Deeply INSPECT the diff\") {\n\t\tt.Error(\"uppercase description keyword should match\")\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestMatches_NoMatchWhenNeitherContains(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\tif skilldiscovery.Matches(\"/format\", \"Reformat code\") {\n\t\tt.Error(\"format/reformat should not match review keywords\")\n\t}\n\tif skilldiscovery.Matches(\"/lint-fix\", \"Auto-fix lint errors\") {\n\t\tt.Error(\"lint is no longer in the keyword set — see spec §Keyword Set\")\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run tests to verify they fail**\n\nRun: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/skilldiscovery/... -run TestMatches -v`\nExpected: FAIL — package / `Matches` do not exist.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Implement `Matches`**\n\nCreate `cmd/entire/cli/agent/skilldiscovery/match.go`:\n```go\n// Package skilldiscovery holds the per-agent registries (curated built-ins,\n// install hints) and the keyword match helper that the `entire review`\n// picker uses to discover review-adjacent skills.\npackage skilldiscovery\n\nimport \"strings\"\n\n// reviewKeywords are the substrings that mark a skill as review-adjacent.\n// Kept narrow on purpose — see the s