{"parentUuid":"e1a34577-f936-4e8b-84a3-279fb5e8aed0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01K8Ey1yzqLBhn9hEukGNMhH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Addressing your Additional Instructions question first:** Yes, that textarea is from PR #1009. Here's the full story.\n\n**What it is:** A custom prompt override, per-agent. Saved in `.entire/settings.json`:\n```json\n{\n  \"review\": {\n    \"claude-code\": {\n      \"skills\": [\"/review\", \"/security-review\"],\n      \"prompt\": \"Focus on data-loss risks first, then run the skills above.\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**How it's used at runtime:** `composeReviewPrompt(cfg)` in `review.go` decides what first message the agent receives:\n\n- **If `prompt` is non-empty:** it's used verbatim.\n- **If `prompt` is empty and `skills` is non-empty:** the default template is composed — `\"Please run these review skills in order:\\n  1. /X\\n  2. /Y\\n\"`.\n- **If both empty:** empty string.\n\n**Where it runs:** The composed prompt is (1) written into the pending-review marker so the agent's `UserPromptSubmit` hook records exactly what was asked, and (2) passed to `launcher.LaunchCmd(ctx, prompt)` as the first argument to `claude`/`codex`/`gemini`. When the agent spawns, that text is delivered as the opening user message — same as if you typed it yourself.\n\nSo: whatever you type in \"Additional instructions\" becomes the **literal text Claude/Codex sees at turn one**.\n\n---\n\nNow back to the pr-review-toolkit miss. Found it: **plugins expose slash commands via `commands/*.md` and subagents via `agents/*.md`**, not `skills/*/SKILL.md`. My walker only handled `skills/`. pr-review-toolkit uses `commands/review-pr.md` and `agents/code-reviewer.md` — neither of which I was scanning.\n\nConcrete on your disk:\n```\n~/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-plugins-official/pr-review-toolkit/unknown/commands/review-pr.md\n~/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/claude-code-plugins/pl