{"parentUuid":"b7cee511-2f87-4d5d-8e8b-3627cca430fb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01UTsz1XczNcR3ukyhegRyu2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Before I dig into detailed questions — quick scope/ambition question, text-only. I'll offer the visual companion later if we hit layout questions.\n\nPhase 2 as you described it is actually a stack of 4-5 features and could itself be phased. Four realistic ambition targets to choose from:\n\n**2a — Multi-agent picker + sequential spawn.**\n`entire review` opens a multi-select picker over your configured agents (today it auto-picks alphabetically-first). Selected agents run **sequentially** — Claude finishes, then Codex, then Gemini — each takes over the TTY as today. No TUI compositor, no parallelism. Ships in days. **Solves your \"only claude starts\" complaint completely**; does not deliver the live-pane UX.\n\n**2b — 2a plus parallel headless spawn + status table.**\nSame multi-select, but agents run **in parallel, headless** (each via its agent's non-interactive mode — `claude --print`, `codex exec`, etc.). `entire` owns a **basic bubbletea TUI** showing one row per agent with status (running / done / failed) and token counters. No Ctrl+O drill-in, no final aggregated summary yet. Ships in a week-ish. Proves the headless plumbing works before investing in the inspection UI.\n\n**2c — 2b plus Ctrl+O inspection + aggregated summary at end.**\nFull UX as you described. Ctrl+O on a row opens a scrollable full-screen view of that agent's transcript-so-far. When all agents finish, a **final synthesis step** runs — either as a simple concatenation, or (bigger ask) by calling one agent one more time to read everyone's outputs and produce a cross-agent review summary. Attach as checkpoint(s) per your \"could also attach\" aside.\n\n**2d — 2c plus \"AI-synthesized\" cross-agent verdict.**\n2c already has aggregation; 2d commits to the \"spawn one more agent call to synthesize\" path as the default, with a user-configurable synthesizer agent. Adds API cost and a whole new concept to the checkpoint model.\n\nMy lean: **phase it as 2a → 2b → 2c**, each shipping independently. Skip 2d unless you find it actually useful after 2c. Starting with 2a alone gets you the UX improvement you hit first today (agent selection) while we build headless plumbing in the background for 2b.\n\nWhich are you aiming for as the Phase 2 deliverable? Or is this one thing that ships together?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7016,"cache_read_input_tokens":425829,"output_tokens":3614,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7016,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":3614,"cache_read_input_tokens":425829,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7016,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7016},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaL4zgSbuffUxhPEnBG3t","type":"assistant","uuid":"b3271940-2a0c-492a-849f-939b5f1a1159","timestamp":"2026-04-23T04:27:44.660Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-review","sessionId":"32ff705a-db92-4346-a9c8-70b631ba581d","version":"2.1.117","gitBranch":"soph/entire-review-2"}
