{"parentUuid":"a2608cd7-dc48-4dce-acfe-907ac964e097","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01QTm1GdrWbLpda126J8h4R5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Verified — Phase 1 is not claude-only, but the spawn default is alphabetically-first.** Details:\n\n- **Configure step (`runReviewConfigPicker`)**: iterates every installed + eligible agent (`review.go:257–307`). If you have claude-code and codex both installed with hooks, the picker offers sections for both agents, saves both to `.entire/settings.json`. Already multi-agent-aware.\n- **Spawn step (`selectReviewAgent`)**: takes `(map[string]ReviewConfig, override string)` and returns ONE agent (`review.go:672`). If `--agent NAME` is passed, uses it; otherwise alphabetically-first. That's what you hit — both agents are *configured*, but only claude-code *launches* because \"c\" < \"g\" < anything else.\n\nSo the fix is at **spawn time**, not configure time. Your phased plan is correct as written. Agreeing with the phasing:\n\n| # | Sub-phase | What ships |\n|---|---|---|\n| **2.1** | Fix spawn picker | Interactive \"which configured agent do you want to run?\" prompt when >1 configured; `--agent` still bypasses |\n| **2.2** | Parallel headless + status table | Multi-select, run agents in parallel via `claude --print` / `codex exec` / etc., basic bubbletea status TUI |\n| **2.3** | Ctrl+O inspection + aggregated summary | Drill-in to one agent's live output; final concatenated summary when all finish |\n| **2.4** | AI-synthesized cross-agent verdict | Spawn one more agent call to read all outputs and produce a meta-review |\n\nEach is its own ship. We'll do **2.1 now** — small, high-value, shippable in a day. Its own spec + plan. Then stop and decide whether to go into 2.2 based on whether 2.1 is enough.\n\n**Next clarifying question (2.1 specifics):**\n\nWhen should the new picker fire?\n\n- **A. Only when >1 agent is configured.** If you only configured claude-code, skip the picker (current fast-path). Only interactive prompt when there's a genuine choice to make. `--agent` still overrides.\n- **B. Always (even with 1 configured).** User sees the picker every run for consistency. Feels chatty when it's a 1-item list.\n- **C. A, but with --no-picker flag** to skip when scripting. So: >1 agent → picker, unless `--agent X` or `--no-picker`.\n\nMy lean: **A**. The picker earns its place when there's a choice; when there isn't, showing a 1-item select is just friction. `--agent` remains the scripting escape hatch.\n\nWhich? Or a different framing?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2785,"cache_read_input_tokens":436619,"output_tokens":1110,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2785,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1110,"cache_read_input_tokens":436619,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2785,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2785},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaL5Ut1Q8ZUiKcStv6jju","type":"assistant","uuid":"852639ff-da8e-4caf-8b8b-785a372bb0cd","timestamp":"2026-04-23T04:33:30.325Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-review","sessionId":"32ff705a-db92-4346-a9c8-70b631ba581d","version":"2.1.117","gitBranch":"soph/entire-review-2"}
