{"parentUuid":"fceb602f-168d-4070-987c-808fab7d686e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01KrRNZbz5mzhNzaXmSZCaRj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good — picker only fires when there's a genuine choice. I think the design is simple enough to present directly. Here it is.\n\n## Sub-phase 2.1 design — \"which agent to run\" picker\n\n### Trigger condition\n\nIn `runReview`, after `selectReviewAgent` logic and before marker write, fire an interactive `huh.Select` *only* when:\n\n```\nlen(eligibleConfigured) > 1 AND agentOverride == \"\"\n```\n\nWhere `eligibleConfigured` = configured agents ∩ agents with hooks installed. (Filtering out hookless-but-configured agents at picker time is friendlier than letting them appear and then erroring.)\n\n- 0 eligible → existing \"hooks not installed\" error, unchanged.\n- 1 eligible → skip picker, proceed to spawn with that agent.\n- 2+ eligible → show picker.\n- `--agent NAME` passed → picker skipped, name must be in `eligibleConfigured`, else error.\n\n### Picker UX\n\n```\nWhich agent should run this review?\n\n> claude-code   (3 skills configured)\n  codex         (1 skill configured)\n  gemini-cli    (prompt-only)\n```\n\nLabel format: `<agent-name>   (<N skills configured> | prompt-only)`. Built from the `ReviewConfig` for each agent. Default selection = alphabetically-first (matches today's silent-default, so Enter-through is behaviorally identical to the pre-2.1 behavior). Ctrl+C = clean exit with silent error, no marker written.\n\n### Refactor\n\nEasiest shape: keep `selectReviewAgent` as-is for single-agent / override paths. Add a new small function `promptForAgent(ctx, eligibleConfigured, out) (string, error)` that runs the huh.Select and returns the picked agent name. In `runReview`:\n\n```go\nif agentOverride == \"\" && len(eligibleConfigured) > 1 {\n    agentOverride, err = promptForAgent(ctx, eligibleConfigured, cmd.OutOrStdout())\n    if err != nil { return err }\n}\n// Fall through to existing selectReviewAgent(review, agentOverride)\n```\n\nThat way the picker result becomes an in-memory `--agent` equivalent, and the rest of `runReview` is untouched.\n\n### Interaction with re-run guard\n\nThe existing re-run guard (\"Already reviewed: X. Proceed anyway?\") fires *after* agent selection. Keep that order — the guard asks about HEAD's checkpoint and is agent-agnostic, so it doesn't matter which agent got picked.\n\n### Testing\n\nThree unit tests plus a small refactor-safety test:\n\n- `TestPromptForAgent_SingleEligibleSkipsPicker` — 1 eligible → returns that name without prompting.\n- `TestPromptForAgent_FlagOverrideSkipsPicker` — `agentOverride` non-empty → picker not called.\n- `TestPromptForAgent_FlagOverrideMustBeEligible` — `--agent foo` where foo isn't eligible → error listing eligible options.\n- `TestRunReview_MultiAgentConfiguredWithFlagSelectsCorrect` — integration-style: 2 configured, `--agent codex`, marker written with AgentName=codex. (Current codebase already has scaffolding for this via `testAgentName` constants.)\n\nThe interactive-picker path (huh TUI) isn't unit-testable headlessly; manual smoke during `entire review` is how it gets exercised, same as the Phase 1 config picker.\n\n### Files touched\n\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/review.go` — add `promptForAgent`, wire into `runReview`.\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/review_test.go` — add the 4 tests above.\n\nEstimated diff: ~120 lines across 2 files. One commit.\n\n---\n\nDoes this shape look right? Anything to change — especially around the label format (N skills configured / prompt-only), the default-selection behavior, or whether you want a `--no-picker` flag too?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1112,"cache_read_input_tokens":439404,"output_tokens":3063,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cac