{"parentUuid":"7c6d80fc-4326-4bde-bb30-fdcf14044c6f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01FRMKe1Xgij6xUuurRvkPgT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015s7aCNocm6UNF5tuTXJKJQ","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-review/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-04-22-entire-review-spawn-agent-picker.md","content":"# `entire review` Spawn-Time Agent Picker — Implementation Plan\n\n> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (if subagents available) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.\n\n**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-22-entire-review-spawn-agent-picker-design.md`\n\n**Goal:** When `entire review` is run with more than one eligible (configured + hooks-installed) agent and no `--agent` flag, prompt the user to pick which agent runs instead of silently defaulting to alphabetical-first.\n\n**Architecture:** Small addition to `cmd/entire/cli/review.go`: a `promptForAgent` helper using `NewAccessibleForm(huh.NewSelect[string]())`, a tiny `runReviewDeps` struct with a `promptForAgentFn` injection hook for testing, and a pre-check in `runReview` that computes the three-way `eligibleConfigured` set and invokes the picker only when len > 1 and no override is set. `selectReviewAgent` is unchanged.\n\n**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26.x, Cobra, huh, `mise`/`golangci-lint`/Vogon canary for CI.\n\n**Branch strategy:** Add one commit directly on top of `soph/entire-review-2` (PR #1009). No new branch.\n\n---\n\n## Preamble — confirm base branch state\n\n- [ ] **P.1: Verify working branch is `soph/entire-review-2`**\n\nRun: `git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD`\nExpected: `soph/entire-review-2`. If anything else, stop and switch before continuing.\n\n- [ ] **P.2: Verify Phase 1 state landed**\n\nRun:\n```bash\ngrep -n \"func selectReviewAgent\\|func verifyConfiguredSkillsInstalled\\|func confirmFirstRunSetup\" cmd/entire/cli/review.go\ngrep -n \"CuratedBuiltinsFor\\|IsEligible\\b\" cmd/entire/cli/agent/skilldiscovery/registry.go\n```\nExpected: all symbols present. If any missing, the base branch is wrong — stop and re-confirm.\n\n- [ ] **P.3: Baseline `mise run check`**\n\nRun: `mise run check`\nExpected: PASS. Baselines the tree so failures below are caused by our changes, not pre-existing.\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 1 — spawn-time agent picker\n\nOne commit at the end of this chunk.\n\n### Files\n\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/review.go`\n  - Add type `agentChoice struct { Name, Label string }`\n  - Add type `runReviewDeps` with a `promptForAgentFn func(ctx context.Context, eligible []agentChoice) (string, error)` field\n  - Add `promptForAgent(ctx, eligible)` real implementation (huh.Select + NewAccessibleForm)\n  - Add `computeEligibleConfigured(ctx, s *settings.EntireSettings)` helper that returns `[]agentChoice` sorted alphabetically by Name\n  - Refactor `runReview` to accept dependencies (default = production wiring) and insert the pre-check before `selectReviewAgent`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/review_test.go`\n  - Add 4 test functions listed in the spec\n\n### Task 1 — Implement the picker + wiring + tests\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing unit tests**\n\nAppend to `cmd/entire/cli/review_test.go`:\n```go\n// TestPromptForAgent_SingleEligibleSkipsPicker: when only one agent is\n// configured AND has hooks, the picker never fires and runReview proceeds\n// directly to spawn. Uses the runReviewDeps injection so the stubbed\n// promptForAgentFn would fail the test if it got called.\nfunc TestPromptForAgent_SingleEligibleSkipsPicker(t *testing.T) {\n\tsetupReviewTestRepoWithCommit(t)\n\tinstallHooksForTest(t, testAgentName)\n\n\tif err := saveReviewConfig(context.Background(), map[string]settings.ReviewConfig{\n\t\ttestAgentName: {Prompt: \"review the diff\"},\n\t}); err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\n\tcalled := false\n\tdeps := runReviewDeps{\n\t\tpromptForAgentFn: func(_ context.Context, _ []agentChoice) (string, error) {\n\t\t\tcalled = true\n\t\t\treturn \"\", nil\n\t\t},\n\t}\n\n\trootCmd := NewRootCmdWithDeps(deps) // helper added in Step 3\n\trootCmd.SetArgs([]string{\"review\"})\n\tif err := rootCmd.Execute(); err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\tif called {\n\t\tt.Error(\"promptForAgentFn should not be called when only one eligible agent is configured\")\n\t}\n}\n\n// TestPromptForAgent_FlagOverrideSkipsPicker: when --agent is passed, the\n// picker is skipped even with multiple eligible agents configured.\nfunc TestPromptForAgent_FlagOverrideSkipsPicker(t *testing.T) {\n\tsetupReviewTestRepoWithCommit(t)\n\tinstallHooksForTest(t, testAgentName)\n\tinstallHooksForTest(t, testCodexAgent)\n\n\tif err := saveReviewConfig(context.Background(), map[string]settings.ReviewConfig{\n\t\ttestAgentName:  {Prompt: \"review the diff\"},\n\t\ttestCodexAgent: {Prompt: \"review the diff\"},\n\t}); err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\n\tcalled := false\n\tdeps := runReviewDeps{\n\t\tpromptForAgentFn: func(_ context.Context, _ []agentChoice) (string, error) {\n\t\t\tcalled = true\n\t\t\treturn \"\", nil\n\t\t},\n\t}\n\n\trootCmd := NewRootCmdWithDeps(deps)\n\trootCmd.SetArgs([]string{\"review\", \"--agent\", testCodexAgent})\n\tif err := rootCmd.Execute(); err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\tif called {\n\t\tt.Error(\"promptForAgentFn should not be called when --agent is passed\")\n\t}\n\n\tm, ok, err := ReadPendingReviewMarker(context.Background())\n\tif err != nil || !ok {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"marker should be written: ok=%v err=%v\", ok, err)\n\t}\n\tif m.AgentName != testCodexAgent {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"AgentName = %q, want %s\", m.AgentName, testCodexAgent)\n\t}\n}\n\n// TestPromptForAgent_FlagOverrideMustBeEligibleAgent: the --agent NAME path\n// still gets validated by selectReviewAgent (eligibility-wise) + the\n// existing hooks-installed gate. This test pins that a configured-but-\n// hookless --agent name surfaces a clear error rather than silently\n// picking a different agent.\nfunc TestPromptForAgent_FlagOverrideMustBeEligibleAgent(t *testing.T) {\n\tsetupReviewTestRepoWithCommit(t)\n\tinstallHooksForTest(t, testAgentName)\n\t// Configure codex too but do NOT install its hooks.\n\n\tif err := saveReviewConfig(context.Background(), map[string]settings.ReviewConfig{\n\t\ttestAgentName:  {Prompt: \"review the diff\"},\n\t\ttestCodexAgent: {Prompt: \"review the diff\"},\n\t}); err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\n\trootCmd := NewRootCmd()\n\terrBuf := &bytes.Buffer{}\n\trootCmd.SetErr(errBuf)\n\trootCmd.SetArgs([]string{\"review\", \"--agent\", testCodexAgent})\n\terr := rootCmd.Execute()\n\tif err == nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(\"expected error when --agent points at hookless agent\")\n\t}\n\tif !strings.Contains(errBuf.String(), \"Hooks are not installed\") {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"stderr should mention 'Hooks are not installed', got: %s\", errBuf.String())\n\t}\n}\n\n// TestRunReview_MultiAgentNoFlagTriggersPicker: canonical picker-fires path.\n// Two eligible agents, no flag, stubbed promptForAgentFn returns the\n// second (alphabetically) → marker written with that agent.\nfunc TestRunReview_MultiAgentNoFlagTriggersPicker(t *testing.T) {\n\tsetupReviewTestRepoWithCommit(t)\n\tinstallHooksForTest(t, testAgentName)\n\tinstallHooksForTest(t, testCodexAgent)\n\n\tif err := saveReviewConfig(context.Background(), map[string]settings.ReviewConfig{\n\t\ttestAgentName:  {Prompt: \"review the diff\"},\n\t\ttestCodexAgent: {Prompt: \"review the diff\"},\n\t}); err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\n\tvar seen []string\n\tdeps := runReviewDeps{\n\t\tpromptForAgentFn: func(_ context.Context, eligible []agentChoice) (string, error) {\n\t\t\tfor _, e := range eligible {\n\t\t\t\tseen = append(seen, e.Name)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t// eligible is sorted alphabetically; pick the second one.\n\t\t\tif len(eligible) < 2 {\n\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"expected >=2 eligible, got %d\", len(eligible))\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn eligible[1].Name, nil\n\t\t},\n\t}\n\n\trootCmd := NewRootCmdWithDeps(deps)\n\trootCmd.SetArgs([]string{\"review\"})\n\tif err := rootCmd.Execute(); err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\n\t// Eligible list should have come in sorted. claude-code < codex alphabetically.\n\tif len(seen) < 2 || seen[0] != testAgentName || seen[1] != testCodexAgent {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"eligible presented to picker = %v, want [%s %s]\", seen, testAgentName, testCodexAgent)\n\t}\n\n\tm, ok, err := ReadPendingReviewMarker(context.Background())\n\tif err != nil || !ok {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"marker should be written: ok=%v err=%v\", ok, err)\n\t}\n\t// Picker returned eligible[1] which is testCodexAgent.\n\tif m.AgentName != testCodexAgent {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"AgentName = %q, want %s\", m.AgentName, testCodexAgent)\n\t}\n}\n```\n\nNote on constants: `testCodexAgent` already exists in `review_test.go` (added in PR #1009). `testAgentName` is the existing Claude Code constant. No new constants needed.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run tests to verify they fail**\n\nRun: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli -run \"TestPromptForAgent|TestRunReview_MultiAgentNoFlag\" -v`\nExpected: FAIL — `runReviewDeps` undefined, `NewRootCmdWithDeps` undefined, `agentChoice` undefined.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Add the injection-hook types and the test helper**\n\nEdit `cmd/entire/cli/review.go`:\n\nAdd near the top of the file (after imports), before any existing function definitions:\n```go\n// agentChoice is one row in the spawn-time picker. Name is the agent\n// registry key (used for marker/override); Label is the picker-visible\n// string (\"<name>   (N skills configured)\" or \"<name>   (prompt-only)\").\ntype agentChoice struct {\n\tName  string\n\tLabel string\n}\n\n// runReviewDeps collects the runtime-injectable hooks runReview uses. Tests\n// stub fields on this struct to drive branches that would otherwise require\n// a real TTY. Production wiring leaves fields nil and defaults are resolved\n// inside runReview.\ntype runReviewDeps struct {\n\tpromptForAgentFn func(ctx context.Context, eligible []agentChoice) (string, error)\n}\n```\n\nAdd a `NewRootCmdWithDeps` alongside the existing `NewRootCmd`. Look for the current `NewRootCmd` in `root.go` (not `review.go`). If there's no existing DI pattern, the cleanest shape is:\n\n1. Keep `NewRootCmd()` returning the real command tree using production `runReviewDeps{}` (zero-valued, which resolves to real `promptForAgent`).\n2. Add `NewRootCmdWithDeps(deps runReviewDeps)` that threads the deps into only the review command. This is test-only API, lowercase `reviewCmd` constructors can accept an optional `deps` param.\n\n**Important:** if `NewRootCmd` lives in a different file and is load-bearing for many other tests, do NOT refactor its signature. Instead add a focused test-only helper in `review_test.go` that constructs the review subcommand directly with the injected deps, bypassing `NewRootCmd`. The tests above can be adjusted to call this helper if wiring through `NewRootCmd` would sprawl. Prefer the smaller-blast-radius option.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Implement `promptForAgent` and `computeEligibleConfigured`**\n\nAdd to `cmd/entire/cli/review.go`:\n```go\n// computeEligibleConfigured returns agents that are (a) configured with a\n// non-zero ReviewConfig and (b) have hooks installed, sorted alphabetically\n// by name. Each entry's Label is the picker-visible string derived from\n// the ReviewConfig.\nfunc computeEligibleConfigured(ctx context.Context, s *settings.EntireSettings) []agentChoice {\n\tif s == nil {\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\tinstalled := GetAgentsWithHooksInstalled(ctx)\n\tinstalledSet := make(map[types.AgentName]struct{}, len(installed))\n\tfor _, name := range installed {\n\t\tinstalledSet[name] = struct{}{}\n\t}\n\tvar out []agentChoice\n\tfor name, cfg := range s.Review {\n\t\tif cfg.IsZero() {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif _, ok := installedSet[types.AgentName(name)]; !ok {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tout = append(out, agentChoice{Name: name, Label: labelForAgentChoice(name, cfg)})\n\t}\n\tsort.Slice(out, func(i, j int) bool { return out[i].Name < out[j].Name })\n\treturn out\n}\n\n// labelForAgentChoice renders the picker label for one agent.\nfunc labelForAgentChoice(name string, cfg settings.ReviewConfig) string {\n\tswitch {\n\tcase len(cfg.Skills) > 0:\n\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%s   (%d skills configured)\", name, len(cfg.Skills))\n\tcase cfg.Prompt != \"\":\n\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%s   (prompt-only)\", name)\n\tdefault:\n\t\t// cfg.IsZero() callers already filter this case out; defensive.\n\t\treturn name\n\t}\n}\n\n// promptForAgent runs a single-select huh picker over the given eligible\n// agents and returns the picked name. Uses NewAccessibleForm so the form\n// respects ACCESSIBLE=1 per CLAUDE.md.\nfunc promptForAgent(ctx context.Context, eligible []agentChoice) (string, error) {\n\t_ = ctx\n\tif len(eligible) == 0 {\n\t\treturn \"\", errors.New(\"no eligible agents to prompt for\")\n\t}\n\toptions := make([]huh.Option[string], 0, len(eligible))\n\tfor _, c := range eligible {\n\t\toptions = append(options, huh.NewOption(c.Label, c.Name))\n\t}\n\t// Default selection = alphabetically first, matching the pre-2.1\n\t// silent-default behavior so Enter-through users land on the same\n\t// agent they did before.\n\tpicked := eligible[0].Name\n\tform := NewAccessibleForm(huh.NewGroup(\n\t\thuh.NewSelect[string]().\n\t\t\tTitle(\"Which agent should run this review?\").\n\t\t\tOptions(options...).\n\t\t\tValue(&picked),\n\t))\n\tif err := form.Run(); err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"agent picker: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\treturn picked, nil\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Wire the pre-check into `runReview`**\n\nFind the block in `runReview` around the call to `selectReviewAgent(s.Review, agentOverride)` (currently `review.go:672`-ish). Before that call, insert:\n```go\n// Spawn-time agent picker: when multiple agents are configured AND have\n// hooks installed, give the user an interactive choice. Skip when only\n// one is eligible (fast path) or when --agent already narrows it down.\nif agentOverride == \"\" {\n\teligible := computeEligibleConfigured(ctx, s)\n\tif len(eligible) > 1 {\n\t\tfn := deps.promptForAgentFn\n\t\tif fn == nil {\n\t\t\tfn = promptForAgent\n\t\t}\n\t\tpicked, err := fn(ctx, eligible)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\tcmd.SilenceUsage = true\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprintln(cmd.ErrOrStderr(), err.Error())\n\t\t\treturn NewSilentError(err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tagentOverride = picked\n\t}\n}\n```\n\nThread `deps runReviewDeps` through `runReview`'s signature. If this is the first time `runReview` takes deps, update its existing caller in `review.go` (`newReviewCmd`) to pass a zero-valued `runReviewDeps{}`. The `newReviewCmd` constructor can take an optional deps parameter with a zero default, or a builder can be used — match whatever is least invasive.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Run the four unit tests**\n\nRun: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli -run \"TestPromptForAgent|TestRunReview_MultiAgentNoFlag\" -v`\nExpected: PASS.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Run the broader review test suite + lint**\n\nRun:\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli -run \"TestReview|TestRunReview|TestMergePickerResults|TestComposeReviewPrompt|TestPromptForAgent\" -v\nmise run fmt && mise run lint\n```\nExpected: all tests pass; `mise run fmt` idempotent; `mise run lint` reports 0 issues. If `fmt` changes anything, re-run `lint` after.\n\nIf lint fires on the new code, common gotchas from Phase 1:\n- `err113` / `perfsprint` — prefer `errors.New(\"literal\")` or `%w` wrapping; plan uses both idiomatically above.\n- `unparam` — `promptForAgent` currently accepts `ctx` without using it; if flagged, drop the `_ = ctx` discard line and either use it or add `//nolint:unparam`. Prefer using it; `huh` may not take context, but we can `ctx.Err()` before the `form.Run()` for cancel-friendliness.\n- `inamedparam` — huh interface assertions sometimes require named receivers.\n\nApply the same patterns Phase 1 used in `review.go` — match the style that's already there.\n\n### Chunk 1 end — local build + commit\n\n- [ ] **Step 8: Full local build**\n\nRun: `mise run check`\nExpected: PASS (fmt, lint, unit, integration, Vogon canary).\n\n- [ ] **Step 9: Duplication scan**\n\nRun: `mise run dup`\nExpected: no new duplicates from `promptForAgent`, `computeEligibleConfigured`, or `labelForAgentChoice`. If `computeEligibleConfigured` gets flagged against an existing helper, replace local impl.\n\n- [ ] **Step 10: Commit**\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/review.go cmd/entire/cli/review_test.go\ngit commit -m \"Prompt for review agent when multiple are configured\"\n```\n\nExpected: commit succeeds. One commit for the whole sub-phase.\n\n---\n\n## Done\n\nImplementation complete when:\n\n- `mise run check` is green on the new tip.\n- The four new tests pass in the normal suite.\n- Manual smoke: in a repo with both claude-code AND codex configured (both with hooks), `entire review` prompts \"Which agent should run this review?\" and launches the picked agent. With only one configured, no prompt — direct spawn. With `--agent codex`, no prompt — spawn codex.\n- No new commits beyond this one; still a single-commit sub-phase.\n\n## Acceptance criteria (spec → plan mapping)\n\n| Spec requirement | Plan coverage |\n|---|---|\n| `promptForAgent(ctx, eligible) (string, error)` helper | Task 1, Step 4 |\n| `runReviewDeps.promptForAgentFn` injection hook | Task 1, Step 3 |\n| Three-way eligibility filter (configured + non-zero + hooks) | Task 1, Step 4 (`computeEligibleConfigured`) |\n| `NewAccessibleForm` wrapping | Task 1, Step 4 (`promptForAgent` body) |\n| Default selection = alphabetical-first | Task 1, Step 4 (`picked := eligible[0].Name`) |\n| Title exactly \"Which agent should run this review?\" | Task 1, Step 4 |\n| Label format with skills count or prompt-only | Task 1, Step 4