{"parentUuid":"289a6e73-530c-4d95-bc34-3d7dcafc330d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01LuXMypnUxHZJg2V4Ehh168","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"B locked. Next unknown is forced by reality not taste.\n\n**Question 3 — agents without headless mode.** Not every agent we register has a non-interactive flag. As far as I know:\n\n| Agent | Headless command | Known |\n|---|---|---|\n| claude-code | `claude --print \"<prompt>\"` | ✅ yes |\n| codex | `codex exec \"<prompt>\"` | ✅ yes |\n| gemini-cli | `gemini -p \"<prompt>\"` (or `-i`) | ✅ yes |\n| cursor | — | ❌ no (IDE only) |\n| opencode | ? | probably yes, needs verify |\n| factoryai-droid | ? | unknown |\n| copilot-cli | ? | unknown |\n\nIn 2.1 today, agents without `Launcher` (cursor, opencode, factoryai-droid in the current code) fall through the `!ok` path and just instruct the user to start the agent manually. In 2.2 that's not viable — a parallel-run TUI can't accommodate \"go manually start codex in another terminal\". So two options for handling these agents:\n\n- **A. Filter them out of the multi-select picker entirely.** A new capability interface `HeadlessLauncher` (extending/alongside `Launcher`) — only agents implementing it appear in the 2.2 picker. An agent configured for review but without headless just doesn't show up as a multi-run option. (Still works with Phase 2.1's single-agent picker.)\n- **B. Show them but error clearly if selected.** Picker shows all configured, selecting a non-headless one prints `\"agent <name> doesn't support parallel review; use \"entire review --agent <name>\" to run it interactively\"`. Slightly friendlier discovery but more error paths.\n\nMy lean: **A**. Keeps the multi-select honest — everything the user can pick will actually work. The interactive-only agents are still reachable via 2.1's single-agent path (`entire review --agent cursor` → TTY hand-off, same as today).\n\nAlso worth confirming: does