{"parentUuid":"13c9368a-753f-41cf-aff4-83275d015e31","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"75c0981c-be7b-4e38-909c-0dccb9db8366","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015FHqSTw3d9Fn9rxcKsUjkw","type":"tool_result","content":"# GitHub Copilot CLI Commands & Non-Interactive Mode\n\n## Main Commands\n\nThe CLI offers these primary commands:\n- `copilot` — Interactive UI\n- `copilot login` — Authentication\n- `copilot init` — Repository setup\n- `copilot version` — Version info\n- `copilot update` — Install latest version\n- `copilot mcp` / `copilot plugin` — Configuration management\n\n## Non-Interactive Agent Mode\n\nYes, there is a programmatic mode. You can invoke the CLI with a prompt that executes without launching the interactive interface:\n\n> \"-p PROMPT, --prompt=PROMPT: Execute a prompt programmatically (exits after completion)\"\n\nAdditionally, you can use:\n\n> \"-i PROMPT, --interactive=PROMPT: Start an interactive session and automatically execute this prompt\"\n\nThe `-p` flag is designed specifically for scripting and automation scenarios. When used, the CLI processes your prompt and exits automatically.\n\n## Related Flags\n\nFor programmatic use, these flags are relevant:\n- `--silent` — Output only the agent response (useful for scripting)\n- `--allow-all-tools` — Required for programmatic operation\n- `--output-format=FORMAT` — Choose `text` or `json` (outputs JSONL format)\n\nThere are no `--print`, `--exec`, or `--batch` flags documented in this reference.\n\n## Hook Support\n\nYes, hooks fire during programmatic execution. The documented hook events include `userPromptSubmitted`, `preToolUse`, `postToolUse`, `agentStop`, and others that would activate during automated task completion."}]},"uuid":"10b68e3d-fed8-4127-8da6-47dd6a10c800","timestamp":"2026-04-23T06:05:06.714Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":143854,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# GitHub Copilot CLI Commands & Non-Interactive Mode\n\n## Main Commands\n\nThe CLI offers these primary commands:\n- `copilot` — Interactive UI\n- `copilot login` — Authentication\n- `copilot init` — Repository setup\n- `copilot version` — Version info\n- `copilot update` — Install latest version\n- `copilot mcp` / `copilot plugin` — Configuration management\n\n## Non-Interactive Agent Mode\n\nYes, there is a programmatic mode. You can invoke the CLI with a prompt that executes without launching the interactive interface:\n\n> \"-p PROMPT, --prompt=PROMPT: Execute a prompt programmatically (exits after completion)\"\n\nAdditionally, you can use:\n\n> \"-i PROMPT, --interactive=PROMPT: Start an interactive session and automatically execute this prompt\"\n\nThe `-p` flag is designed specifically for scripting and automation scenarios. When used, the CLI processes your prompt and exits automatically.\n\n## Related Flags\n\nFor programmatic use, these flags are relevant:\n- `--silent` — Output only the agent response (useful for scripting)\n- `--allow-all-tools` — Required for programmatic operation\n- `--output-format=FORMAT` — Choose `text` or `json` (outputs JSONL format)\n\nThere are no `--print`, `--exec`, or `--batch` flags documented in this reference.\n\n## Hook Support\n\nYes, hooks fire during programmatic execution. The documented hook events include `userPromptSubmitted`, `preToolUse`, `postToolUse`, `agentStop`, and others that would activate during automated task completion.","durationMs":5465,"url":"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/reference/copilot-cli-reference/cli-command-reference"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"13c9368a-753f-41cf-aff4-83275d015e31","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-review","sessionId":"32ff705a-db92-4346-a9c8-70b631ba581d","version":"2.1.117","gitBranch":"soph/entire-review-2"}
