{"parentUuid":"c5ddb894-7b3e-45f8-af8f-eecc9ba7efe1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Xpk5mfR3FkfE6F4DRNEV5q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good correction — and better news than I thought. The repo already has headless invocation plumbing for text generation:\n\n- **Cursor:** `cursor-agent --print --force --trust --workspace <dir>` — used by `cursor/generate.go` for text generation today.\n- **Copilot CLI:** `copilot -p \"<prompt>\" --allow-all-tools --silent` — hooks fire (userPromptSubmitted, agentStop).\n- **Claude Code:** `claude --print`.\n- **Codex:** `codex exec`.\n- **Gemini:** `gemini -p` (expected, `geminicli/generate.go` handles this shape).\n- **opencode / factoryai-droid:** unknown but presumably similar — they have `generate.go` in the repo too.\n\nSo realistically, **most configured agents already have the headless plumbing**. We're not inventing it — we're re-targeting the same invocation pattern that `GenerateText` (used for compact transcripts, summaries) already uses. A new capability interface `HeadlessLauncher` would be shaped like:\n\n```go\ntype HeadlessLauncher interface {\n    Agent\n    // Stdio left unwired so caller can pipe/capture for the TUI.\n    LaunchHeadlessCmd(ctx context.Context, initialPrompt string) (*exec.Cmd, error)\n}\n```\n\nAnd the filter becomes \"configured ∩ hooks-installed ∩ implements `HeadlessLauncher`\".\n\n**Confirming direction: A (filter) stays my answer**, but now it's less of a forced hack and more of a principled capability check — agents that don't implement `HeadlessLauncher` simply aren't offered for multi-agent runs. They still work in 2.1's single-agent TTY-handoff path. Sound good?\n\nIf yes, next question is about **cancellation + failure handling** — one agent dies, do the others keep going, do we fail-fast, or do we prompt? And does Ctrl+C kill all or ask first?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":