{"parentUuid":"b66273c8-7093-4ece-9711-68a20713ee68","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01XGdzQrmcyK7c1gK8XEhxJ7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Last design question, then I present the full thing.\n\n**Question 5 — what happens when all agents finish?** The TUI's final paint is on screen. Four possibilities:\n\n- **A. Exit immediately.** TUI quits as soon as the last agent returns. Terminal retains the final table state (bubbletea's default on quit). User can scroll up to see it later.\n- **B. Pause on completion screen until user hits a key.** Gives a moment to read before the prompt comes back. Annoying if you want to move on fast.\n- **C. Exit with a one-line summary.** Leaves the table state visible + prints `\"3 agents done in 2m 14s (3 succeeded, 0 failed). Run git commit to attach the review to the next checkpoint.\"` The closing line points the user at the right next step.\n- **D. Start the Ctrl+O / aggregated view.** No — that's 2.3's scope, not 2.2.\n\nMy lean: **C**. Same ergonomics as a CI runner: dashboard stays visible, one line tells you what to do next. No extra keypress required.\n\nA also works if you prefer terseness — just the table, no closing line. B feels dated.\n\nC / A / different?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1227,"cache_read_input_tokens":532644,"output_tokens":802,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1227},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":802,"cache_read_input_tokens":532644,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1227,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1227,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaLCuSt4osi198NggbTu2","type":"assistant","uuid":"9e33e890-a8c0