{"parentUuid":"35023b4a-665d-40b5-a6b0-96739b2c2017","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_014VE9jm5SzrxuXUmhMNXDwZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Right — \"full output\" really means tool calls, thinking, intermediate messages, etc., not just the final response text. There are actually two \"fulls\" in play:\n\n1. **Final response text** — what the agent *said* at the end. That's what my \"dump on completion\" shows.\n2. **Full uncompacted transcript** — every tool call, every intermediate thought, every message. Way more verbose. Usually 10–100× the final response.\n\nThe good news: **entire already captures #2 today, in every agent's native transcript format.** Each agent's hook-driven session record points at a file on disk (`~/.claude/projects/<repo>/<session>.jsonl` for claude, `~/.codex/sessions/...` for codex, etc.). Once an agent finishes, that file is complete. We don't need to build transcript capture — we need to surface where it lives.\n\n**Proposed 2.2 completion output:**\n\n```\n─────── claude-code review ───────\n[full final response text]\n\n─────── codex review ───────\n[full final response text]\n\n─────── gemini-cli review ───────\n[full final response text]\n\n✓ 3 agents done in 2m 14s (3 succeeded, 0 failed)\n  Run `git commit` to attach the review to the next checkpoint.\n\n  Full transcripts (including tool calls + reasoning):\n    claude-code → ~/.claude/projects/-Users-peyton-myrepo/abc-123.jsonl\n    codex       → ~/.codex/sessions/xyz-456.jsonl\n    gemini-cli  → ~/.gemini/tmp/uvw-789/session.jsonl\n```\n\nUser gets three levels of detail on demand:\n\n- **During run:** dashboard preview line (single truncated tail).\n- **On completion:** final response text, inline.\n- **On demand, post-run:** `less <transcript-path>` gives them everything uncompacted. Or the agent's own UI can open it (`claude --resume <session>` etc.). Or later in 2.3, Ctrl+O live-drill, or `entire explain <session>` once we wire that to show the transcript inline.\n\nThis keeps 2.2 focused — we're not writing a new transcript viewer, just pointing at files that already exist. 2.3 can add in-CLI viewing if that path is painful enough to warrant it.\n\nSound right? Or do you want 2.2 to also write a `.entire/logs/review-<timestamp>/<agent>.log` mirror of stdout in plain text, so users don't have to parse the agent-native JSONL?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2619,"cache_read_input_tokens":538058,"output_tokens":2849,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2619},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":2849,"cache_read_input_tokens":538058,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2619,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2619,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaLDHxUfLv2qPh6nEp4MZ","type":"assistant","uuid":"52a9771f-14b9-4da9-89ff-7b661f13b3ab","timestamp":"2026-04-23T06:16:19.713Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-review","sessionId":"32ff705a-db92-4346-a9c8-70b631ba581d","version":"2.1.117","gitBranch":"soph/entire-review-2"}
