{"parentUuid":"7727ee42-c0da-4cba-b4f8-bcb4ce8fa663","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01VwtNXeZ54H1sydytFzkk8g","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Clear now — you want confirmation the dump is actually the full final response, not some compacted version. It is. The agent's final response text is emitted to stdout as-is when it finishes; we buffer it during the run (for the preview line) and print the full buffer on exit. No truncation, no summarization, no entire-side compaction of that text.\n\nConcretely, the preview and the dump are two different things:\n\n- **Preview line during run:** `…last-line-of-stdout-truncated-to-fit-row-width` — visual peek only.\n- **Dump on completion:** `os.Stdout.Write(agentBuffer)` or equivalent — every byte the agent printed, exactly as it was printed.\n\nAny internal \"compact transcript\" flow in the repo is a different pipeline (used when we call an agent for summaries / meta work, sends a reduced transcript to save tokens). The final-response-text-as-printed is never run through that — it's just bytes captured from a pipe.\n\nSo the full plan for 2.2 is:\n\n1. Multi-select picker\n2. Parallel headless spawn with `HeadlessLauncher` capability filter\n3. bubbletea TUI: row per agent, live spinner + duration + tokens (if available per agent)\n4. Live preview line (truncated last-line of stdout) per row during run\n5. Per-agent independent failure; others keep going\n6. Graceful SIGTERM on first Ctrl+C, SIGKILL on second\n7. One shared marker `review-pending.json` with `agent_names[]` + adoption refcount; one multi-session checkpoint on next commit\n8. On completion: exit TUI, dump each agent's **full final response** sequentially, print summary + transcript paths.\n\nThat's the design. Any changes before I write it up?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":41,"cache_read_input