{"parentUuid":"b8144556-e6de-4c36-a2bf-5b95833e7831","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_0152UinjsQzLtTnYESwutMru","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Taking that as **option 1** (2.2 ships per-agent only; 2.3/2.4 add the other views). Now the full design, in four sections.\n\n## Section 1 of 4 — Architecture overview\n\n### Components\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  entire review                                                │\n│                                                               │\n│  ┌──────────────┐     ┌──────────────────────────────────┐   │\n│  │ Multi-select │ ──► │  computeEligibleForHeadless()    │   │\n│  │   picker     │     │  (configured ∩ hooks ∩           │   │\n│  │              │     │   implements HeadlessLauncher)    │   │\n│  └──────────────┘     └──────────────────────────────────┘   │\n│         │                                                     │\n│         ▼                                                     │\n│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐    │\n│  │  multiReviewOrchestrator                            │    │\n│  │  ───────────────────────────────                    │    │\n│  │  • Writes shared marker (agent_names, adopted_by)   │    │\n│  │  • Spawns N goroutines (one per selected agent)     │    │\n│  │  • Owns bubbletea tea.Program                       │    │\n│  │  • Handles SIGTERM/SIGKILL cascade on Ctrl+C        │    │\n│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘    │\n│      │                            │                          │\n│      ▼                            ▼                          │\n│  ┌──────────┐                ┌──────────────┐                │\n│  │ per-     │                │ bubbletea    │                │\n│  │ agent    │◄──messages────►│ TUI Model    │                │\n│  │ runners  │  (state changes │ (rows,       │                │\n│  │ (N)      │   stdout lines) │  spinners,   │                │\n│  │          │                 │  preview)    │                │\n│  └──────────┘                 └──────────────┘                │\n│      │                                                        │\n│      ▼                                                        │\n│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐    │\n│  │  On all-done: exit TUI → dump per-agent final       │    │\n│  │  responses → print summary + transcript paths        │    │\n│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘    │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n              (independently, agent hooks fire)\n                        │\n                        ▼\n             ┌──────────────────────────┐\n             │  adoptPendingReviewMarker│\n             │  Into (per-agent hook)   │\n             │                          │\n             │  Reads shared marker,    │\n             │  sees own name in list,  │\n             │  tags session, appends   │\n             │  to adopted_by. Last one │\n             │  clears the marker.      │\n             └──────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Data flow, happy-path\n\n1. User runs `entire review`.\n2. Phase 1/2.1 eligibility runs first. If multi-agent behavior should fire (see below), picker shows **multi-select** over `computeEligibleForHeadless` result.\n3. User picks ≥1 agents. If exactly 1, we drop into 2.1's existing single-agent path (TTY takeover) — no TUI.\n4. If ≥2 picked, orchestrator: writes shared marker, spawns goroutines, starts bubbletea program, blocks on program exit.\n5. Each agent's subprocess runs headlessly (`LaunchHeadlessCmd`); stdout is piped to the orchestrator, which (a) buffers the full text for final dump, (b) emits preview-line messages to the bubbletea Model, (c) tracks exit status.\n6. Independently, each agent's `UserPromptSubmit` hook fires inside its subprocess, reads the shared marker, tags its session, appends to `adopted_by`. Last adopter clears the marker.\n7. When all subprocesses exit, orchestrator sends a \"done\" message to the TUI, which quits. Orchestrator prints per-agent dumps + summary + transcript paths.\n8. User later runs `git commit`; condensation writes one multi-session checkpoint with N entries (existing infrastructure from PR #993).\n\n### When does multi-agent fire?\n\n- `entire review` with 2+ eligible and no `--agent` flag → **multi-select picker** (new). User can pick 1 or more.\n- If picker returns 1 selection → drop into 2.1's single-agent TTY path.\n- If picker returns 2+ selections → orchestrator + TUI.\n- `entire review --agent X` → single-agent path (unchanged from 2.1).\n- `entire review --all` (new flag) → skip picker, select all eligible agents.\n\n### Unit boundaries\n\nSix clear units, each independently testable:\n\n1. **`HeadlessLauncher` interface** + per-agent impls — agent package.\n2. **Shared marker model** — PendingReviewMarker struct extensions + file-locked adoption logic in `review.go`.\n3. **Multi-select picker** — extends `promptForAgent` signature or adds a sibling `promptForAgents` returning `[]string`.\n4. **`multiReviewOrchestrator`** — new file `cmd/entire/cli/review_multi.go`, owns goroutines + signal handling + `tea.Program` lifetime.\n5. **`reviewTUIModel`** — bubbletea `tea.Model` for the status table, no business logic, just rendering + message handling.\n6. **Completion output** — helper that renders the per-agent dumps + summary line.\n\nSection 1 OK, or anything to reshape before I drill into the data model (Section 2)?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":423,"cache_read_input_tokens":551405,"output_tokens":3352,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":423},"inference_geo":"","iter