{"parentUuid":"eed6528f-36bb-445e-9fc5-b55f10bbc718","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01WBFpKrXAfyUrUiHQvus7LD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3363,"cache_read_input_tokens":551828,"output_tokens":4614,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3363},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":4614,"cache_read_input_tokens":551828,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3363,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3363,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaLFGT3JoVfz6CQp4KLyS","type":"assistant","uuid":"9e12f5a7-ed8e-47a4-8588-1bc6464a6e9c","timestamp":"2026-04-23T06:42:10.657Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-review","sessionId":"32ff705a-db92-4346-a9c8-70b631ba581d","version":"2.1.117","gitBranch":"soph/entire-review-2"}
{"parentUuid":"9e12f5a7-ed8e-47a4-8588-1bc6464a6e9c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01WBFpKrXAfyUrUiHQvus7LD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Section 2 of 4 — Data model\n\n### `HeadlessLauncher` capability interface\n\nNew optional interface alongside `Launcher` (which stays untouched for 2.1's TTY path):\n\n```go\n// cmd/entire/cli/agent/agent.go — add next to Launcher\n\n// HeadlessLauncher is implemented by agents that support running a prompt\n// in non-interactive mode (stdout captured, process exits after response).\n// This is what `entire review`'s multi-agent TUI uses to spawn N parallel\n// reviews. Agents that only support interactive TTY invocation (cursor\n// without --print, opencode if it has no non-interactive mode) simply\n// don't implement this; they remain reachable via 2.1's single-agent path.\n//\n// Contract:\n//   - LaunchHeadlessCmd returns an *exec.Cmd with stdout/stderr pipes\n//     ready to be assigned by the caller (Stdin optional).\n//   - The subprocess must terminate on its own once the prompt completes.\n//   - The agent's UserPromptSubmit hook must fire during the run so the\n//     pending-review marker adoption pipeline works.\ntype HeadlessLauncher interface {\n    Agent\n    LaunchHeadlessCmd(ctx context.Context, initialPrompt string) (*exec.Cmd, error)\n}\n```\n\nPer-agent implementations are thin — most reuse the command shape they already use in `GenerateText` (e.g. Claude uses `claude --print`, Codex uses `codex exec`, Cursor uses `cursor-agent --print --force --trust --workspace`). No new agent-side work beyond returning an `*exec.Cmd` instead of running it directly. Agents that don't support headless simply don't implement the interface.\n\n### `PendingReviewMarker` extension\n\nThe marker gains one field. Everything else stays backwards-compatible:\n\n```go\ntype PendingReviewMarker struct {\n    AgentName    string    `json:\"agent_name,omitempty\"`    // single-agent (Phase 1/2.1)\n    AgentNames   []string  `json:\"agent_names,omitempty\"`   // NEW: multi-agent list\n    Skills       []string  `json:\"skills\"`                  // unchanged\n    Prompt       string    `json:\"prompt,omitempty\"`        // unchanged\n    StartingSHA  string    `json:\"starting_sha\"`            // unchanged\n    StartedAt    time.Time `json:\"started_at\"`              // unchanged\n    WorktreePath string    `json:\"worktree_path,omitempty\"` // unchanged\n}\n```\n\n**Hook adoption logic changes minimally:**\n\n```\nadoptPendingReviewMarkerInto(ctx, state, agentName):\n    read marker\n    if marker.AgentName != \"\":                       # Phase 1 path (unchanged)\n        if AgentName != agentName: leave alone\n        else: tag session, clear marker\n    elif len(marker.AgentNames) > 0:                 # NEW multi-agent path\n        if agentName not in AgentNames: leave alone\n        else: tag session\n              # DO NOT clear marker — orchestrator cleans up\n```\n\nNo concurrent-write problem because hooks don't write back to the marker. The orchestrator owns marker lifecycle:\n\n- Writes the marker before spawning subprocesses.\n- On all-done (happy path) or on cancel / SIGTERM: `defer ClearPendingReviewMarker(ctx)` cleans it up.\n- If orchestrator crashes before cleanup, the marker self-heals on next run via the existing stale-marker handling from Phase 1.\n\nThis is subtler than refcounting but way simpler operationally.\n\n### Multi-select picker\n\nA new helper alongside `promptForAgent`:\n\n```go\n// Returns selected agent names (1+). An empty return is an explicit user\n// cancel — caller should exit silently, no marker written.\nfunc promptForAgents(ctx context.Context, eligible []agentChoice) ([]string, error)\n```\n\nInternally uses `huh.NewMultiSelect[string]()` instead of `NewSelect`. Label format stays `\"<name>   (N skills configured)\"` / `\"<name>   (prompt-only)\"`. Default = no pre-checked options (user actively picks). Ctrl+C during picker → empty slice, `context.Canceled` error.\n\n### `runReviewDeps` additions\n\nTwo new injection hooks for testability:\n\n```go\ntype runReviewDeps struct {\n    promptForAgentFn  func(ctx, []agentChoice) (string, error)       // existing (2.1)\n    promptForAgentsFn func(ctx, []agentChoice) ([]string, error)     // NEW\n    runMultiAgentFn   func(ctx, []MultiAgentTask) (MultiRunResult, error)  // NEW\n}\n```\n\n`runMultiAgentFn` is the full orchestrator entry point. Tests stub it to simulate multi-agent runs without real subprocesses or bubbletea. Production wiring (nil → real function) kicks in when fields are unset, same pattern as 2.1.\n\n### New types\n\n```go\n// Input to the orchestrator — one per selected agent.\ntype MultiAgentTask struct {\n    Agent          agent.HeadlessLauncher\n    Name           string               // agentChoice.Name\n    Prompt         string               // composed prompt (existing composeReviewPrompt)\n    TranscriptPath string               // where the agent writes its native transcript (populated after spawn via hook)\n}\n\n// Output after all agents finish or are cancelled.\ntype MultiRunResult struct {\n    Runs []AgentRunResult  // one per input task, same order\n}\n\ntype AgentRunResult struct {\n    Name         string\n    Status       AgentRunStatus    // Done | Failed | Cancelled\n    ExitCode     int               // 0 if Done\n    Duration     time.Duration\n    FinalOutput  []byte            // full stdout buffer for the completion dump\n    Err          error             // non-nil for Failed / Cancelled with reason\n    TokenUsage   *agent.TokenUsage // nil if agent doesn't emit usable token data\n}\n\ntype AgentRunStatus int\nconst (\n    AgentRunQueued AgentRunStatus = iota\n    AgentRunRunning\n    AgentRunDone\n    AgentRunFailed\n    AgentRunCancelled\n)\n```\n\nAll new types live in the new file `cmd/entire/cli/review_multi.go` (orchestrator home).\n\nSection 2 OK before I do the runtime orchestration + TUI shape (Section 3)?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3363,"cache_read_input_tokens":551828,"output_tokens":4614,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3363},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":4614,"cache_read_input_tokens":551828,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3363,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3363,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaLFGT3JoVfz6CQp4KLyS","type":"assistant","uuid":"29a45e46-d550-442c-8c34-2d9508d0a2ca","timestamp":"2026-04-23T06:42:40.572Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-review","sessionId":"32ff705a-db92-4346-a9c8-70b631ba581d","version":"2.1.117","gitBranch":"soph/entire-review-2"}
