{"parentUuid":"60075bbf-9499-4634-a106-1a4df2edb02e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01QQ9vhMCtmDakkzmErtteBE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed:\n- Origin's `feat/entire-review` tip is now `3b8e0eb0b one more pass on top of feat/entire-review (#1009)` — the squash of all Phase 1 + Sub-phase 2.1 work into one commit on PR #993's branch. PR #1009 is consumed.\n- New base for 2.2: `feat/entire-review` at `3b8e0eb0b`.\n\nBranch name suggestion: **`feat/entire-review-multi-agent`** (matches the repo's `feat/entire-review-*` pattern you used implicitly in earlier commits; shorter `review/multi-agent` also works if you prefer). I'll note whichever you pick in the spec.\n\nI'll switch to the new base and cut the branch once the spec is written — no point doing it mid-brainstorm. Continuing with Section 3.\n\n## Section 3 of 4 — Runtime orchestration + TUI\n\n### Orchestrator lifecycle (`multiReviewOrchestrator`)\n\n```\nmultiReviewOrchestrator.Run(ctx, tasks []MultiAgentTask) (MultiRunResult, error):\n\n    1. Write shared pending-review marker:\n         AgentNames: [task.Name for task in tasks]\n\n    2. Create per-agent channels + buffered stdout writers.\n\n    3. Spawn N goroutines, one per task:\n         cmd := task.Agent.LaunchHeadlessCmd(ctx, task.Prompt)\n         cmd.Stdout = teeWriter(bufForDump, previewChannel)\n         cmd.Stderr = teeWriter(bufForDump, previewChannel)\n         startTime := now()\n         err := cmd.Run()\n         duration := now() - startTime\n         emit AgentRunMsg{Name, Status, Err, FinalOutput, Duration}\n\n    4. Launch tea.Program with reviewTUIModel{tasks, state: all Running}.\n       Messages from goroutines flow into the program via tea.Program.Send.\n\n    5. Wait for program.Run() to return — it quits when all agents\n       report terminal state (Done / Failed / Cancelled) OR when\n       user hits Ctrl+C cascade.\n\n    6. defer ClearPendingReviewMarker(ctx) — cleanup regardless of\n       exit path.\n\n    7. Return MultiRunResult with per-agent final state.\n```\n\n### Cancellation (Ctrl+C)\n\nSignal handling uses the context passed into the orchestrator:\n\n- First Ctrl+C → parent `ctx` gets cancelled → all `exec.CommandContext`-spawned subprocesses receive SIGTERM automatically (Go's context-cancellation → Process.Signal wiring). TUI model flips each running row to `⊘ cancelling…`.\n- Watchdog goroutine: after 5s, if any subprocess hasn't exited, escalate to SIGKILL.\n- Second Ctrl+C within the window → immediate SIGKILL cascade, bypass the 5s grace.\n\nWiring sits in the orchestrator, not in the TUI model — the model only *displays* the cancelling state, doesn't drive it. This keeps the bubbletea Model pure.\n\n### bubbletea `reviewTUIModel`\n\n```go\n// cmd/entire/cli/review_tui.go — new file\n\ntype reviewTUIModel struct {\n    tasks      []MultiAgentTask\n    rows       []rowState                    // one per task\n    spinner    spinner.Model                 // shared spinner for all running rows\n    startTime  time.Time                     // used for live duration counters\n    allDone    bool                          // set when every row is terminal\n}\n\ntype rowState struct {\n    name     string\n    status   AgentRunStatus\n    duration time.Duration                   // final duration; \"now() - startTime\" for running\n    tokens   int                             // 0 if unknown\n    preview  string                          // last truncated line of stdout\n    exitCode int\n}\n\n// Messages consumed:\ntype agentStateChangedMsg struct {\n    name     string\n    status   AgentRunStatus\n    duration time.Duration\n    exitCode int\n}\n\ntype agentPreviewMsg struct {\n    name string\n    line string  // already truncated to terminal width - row prefix - etc.\n}\n\ntype tickMsg time.Time  // bubbletea spinner + duration counter tick\n```\n\nInit/Update/View follow the standard bubbletea `tea.Model` shape. Update handles the three message types (state change, preview, tick). View renders the table + preview lines + bottom status (`N of M complete`). When `allDone` becomes true, Update returns `tea.Quit` to exit cleanly; orchestrator then proceeds to the completion dump.\n\nMinimal rendering — no colors beyond green-done / amber-running / red-failed / gray-dim for preview lines. Matches the mockup.\n\n### Preview line plumbing\n\nEach goroutine's `cmd.Stdout` is set to a `teeWriter`:\n\n```\nteeWriter.Write(p []byte):\n    - Append to buf (for final dump).\n    - Split by \\n; for each complete line:\n          emit agentPreviewMsg{name, strip-ANSI(line), truncated to terminal-width}\n      to the tea.Program via program.Send().\n```\n\nPreview messages are rate-limited (max ~10/sec per agent) so a chatty agent doesn't starve the TUI.\n\n### Completion dump\n\nAfter `tea.Program.Run()` returns and the orchestrator knows every agent is terminal:\n\n```go\nfor i, task := range tasks {\n    result := runs[i]\n    fmt.Fprintf(out, \"\\n─────── %s review ───────\\n\", task.Name)\n    if result.Status == AgentRunFailed {\n        fmt.Fprintf(out, \"(failed — exit %d)\\n\", result.ExitCode)\n        if result.Err != nil {\n            fmt.Fprintf(out, \"%v\\n\", result.Err)\n        }\n    }\n    out.Write(result.FinalOutput)  // the buffered stdout, full + uncompacted\n}\n\nfmt.Fprintln(out)\nfmt.Fprintf(out, \"✓ %d agents done in %s (%d succeeded, %d failed)\\n\",\n    len(tasks), totalDuration, nSucceeded, nFailed)\nfmt.Fprintln(out, \"  Run `git commit` to attach the review to the next checkpoint.\")\nfmt.Fprintln(out)\nfmt.Fprintln(out, \"  Full transcripts (including tool calls + reasoning):\")\nfor _, task := range tasks {\n    if task.TranscriptPath != \"\" {\n        fmt.Fprintf(out, \"    %s → %s\\n\", task.Name, task.TranscriptPath)\n    }\n}\n```\n\n`TranscriptPath` is resolved after the agent's hook fires by reading the session state file the hook creates. If no session was tagged (e.g. agent exited before UserPromptSubmit), that line is omitted — just skipped silently rather than lying.\n\n### New files summary\n\n| File | Purpose | Approx lines |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cmd/entire/cli/review_multi.go` | Orchestrator + types (MultiAgentTask, AgentRunResult, etc.) | ~300 |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/review_tui.go` | bubbletea Model for status table | ~250 |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/review.go` | Extended with multi-select dispatch + `promptForAgents` + new `runReviewDeps` fields | +~120 |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/agent/agent.go` | Add `HeadlessLauncher` interface | +~20 |\n| Per-agent `headless.go` (3-6 new files) | Implement `HeadlessLauncher` for each agent that supports it | ~30 each |\n\nSection 3 OK before Section 4 (testing + non-goals + the final branch & chunking call)?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1507,"cache_read_input_tokens":559865,"output_tokens":3321,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1507},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":3321,"cache_read_input_tokens":559865,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1507,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1507,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaLFXZgpj6tsNgp1KGsJW","type":"assistant","uuid":"e4b44acb-c300-415f-a2ae-e700faac9faf","timestamp":"2026-04-23T06:45:45.215Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-review","sessionId":"32ff705a-db92-4346-a9c8-70b631ba581d","version":"2.1.117","gitBranch":"soph/entire-review-2"}
