{"parentUuid":"4c57de23-270d-46e3-9fce-399cd2dd8bb2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_0187Je2UG2DDubgEcSVvt4qp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done.\n- Simplification committed locally as `2d590f7e1` on `feat/entire-review-simplify` (unpushed, resumable).\n- Now on `feat/entire-review-multi-agent`, tracking `origin/feat/entire-review` at tip `874f9a4ba` (Soph's latest picker fixes included).\n- Phase 2.2 brainstorm resumed.\n\n---\n\n## Section 4 of 4 — Testing + non-goals + chunking call\n\n### Testing strategy\n\nFive concrete test surfaces. The TUI and parallel-spawn code is the hardest to test headlessly, so most coverage goes through the injection hooks.\n\n**Unit tests — `cli/review_test.go`:**\n\n- `TestPromptForAgents_ReturnsSelection` — stubs `runReviewDeps.promptForAgentsFn`, asserts runReview threads the result correctly.\n- `TestPromptForAgents_EmptySelectionCancels` — stubbed picker returns `[]`, runReview exits with silent error, no marker written.\n- `TestMultiReview_PreservesSingleAgentPath` — picker returns exactly 1 selection → drops through to 2.1's single-agent TTY path (no orchestrator, no TUI). Pinned via `runMultiAgentFn` being a sentinel that fails the test if called.\n- `TestMultiReview_OrchestratorReceivesTasks` — picker returns 2+ → stubbed `runMultiAgentFn` receives the right `[]MultiAgentTask` (names, prompts, ordering). Agents not passed to it are the same ones the picker returned.\n\n**Unit tests — new `cli/review_multi_test.go`:**\n\n- `TestOrchestrator_WritesSharedMarker` — with a fake agent interface that never actually runs, assert the marker on disk has `AgentNames: [...]`.\n- `TestOrchestrator_ClearsMarkerOnHappyPathExit` — fake agent exits cleanly, orchestrator defer cleans up marker.\n- `TestOrchestrator_ClearsMarkerOnCancel` — cancel context, fake agents receive cancellation, marker cleaned up.\n- `TestOrchestrator_FailurePerAgentIndependent` — one fake agent returns error, others still complete, final `MultiRunResult` has mixed statuses.\n\n**Unit tests — new `cli/review_tui_test.go`:**\n\n- bubbletea supports `teatest` (from `github.com/charmbracelet/x/exp/teatest`) for headless Model testing.\n- `TestTUIModel_InitialView_AllRowsQueued`.\n- `TestTUIModel_TransitionsToRunningOnStateMsg`.\n- `TestTUIModel_DonePaintAndQuit` — send all-done messages, assert `tea.Quit` returned.\n- `TestTUIModel_PreviewLineTruncates` — preview message with long line → row's preview field is truncated.\n\n**Unit tests — hook adoption with multi-agent marker:**\n\n- `cli/lifecycle_test.go` extension: `TestAdoptMarker_MultiAgentOnly_IgnoresNonListed` — marker has `AgentNames: [A, B]`, a C-agent session hook reads it, doesn't adopt, marker unchanged.\n- `TestAdoptMarker_MultiAgentOnly_DoesNotClearAfterAdopt` — agent A adopts, marker still on disk (orchestrator cleans up, not the hook).\n- `TestAdoptMarker_BackwardsCompat_SingleAgentPath` — existing single-agent marker logic unchanged.\n\n**No new E2E tests.** The existing Vogon canary continues to cover the spawn→adopt→commit loop. Multi-agent-specific E2E would require 2+ real agents running in parallel, which is expensive and fragile — defer until the feature actually ships and real user feedback surfaces a regression we can reproduce.\n\n### Non-goals (explicit — must not leak into this spec)\n\n- **Ctrl+O drill-in during the run** — Sub-phase 2.3.\n- **Aggregated cross-agent summary / AI synthesis** — Sub-phases 2.3 / 2.4.\n- **Streaming stdout peek beyond one-line preview** — 2.3 would add live scrollback; 2.2 caps at one truncated tail per row.\n- **Retrying failed agents** — if one fails, user re-runs manually. No retry button.\n- **Reordering, grouping, or nested agent categories in the picker** — flat multi-select, alphabetical.\n- **Persisting the multi-agent selection across runs** — every run re-prompts (unless `--all` or `--agent NAME`).\n\n### Chunking and branch for implementation\n\nThis is a meaningful ship — 6 unit boundaries, ~1000-1500 LOC net addition. I'd plan **4 chunks**, 1 commit each:\n\n| Chunk | Contents | Approx LOC |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `HeadlessLauncher` interface + per-agent impls (start with Claude Code + Codex + Gemini; cursor + copilot-cli + external-agent support can land in follow-ups) | ~250 |\n| 2 | Multi-select picker (`promptForAgents`) + runReviewDeps extensions + dispatch logic in `runReview` | ~200 |\n| 3 | `multiReviewOrchestrator` (goroutines + shared marker + cancellation) + `PendingReviewMarker.AgentNames` + hook adoption changes | ~350 |\n| 4 | `reviewTUIModel` + bubbletea wiring + preview-line plumbing + completion dump | ~400 |\n\nTarget branch: **`feat/entire-review-multi-agent`** (already checked out, based on `origin/feat/entire-review` at `874f9a4ba`).\n\n### Risks worth flagging now\n\n- **Token counting per row.** The bubbletea status table shows tokens per agent. But only Claude exposes structured token usage in its transcript. For codex/gemini/etc., we'd either leave the column blank (`—`) or scrape from stderr-ish hints. Easiest: display `—` if agent doesn't emit usage; add a capability interface later.\n- **`teatest` dependency.** If it's not already in go.mod, we're adding a test dep. Small but worth noting.\n- **Signal handling on Windows.** `exec.CommandContext` doesn't send SIGTERM on Windows (sends kill). Our graceful-shutdown story needs a platform guard or accept that Windows users get SIGKILL on first Ctrl+C. Not a 2.2 blocker; note in spec.\n- **Parallel subprocesses + concurrent API usage.** If all 3 agents hit the same API provider simultaneously, rate limits could bite. Not our concern operationally, but worth a warning in the dashboard if we get a provider 429 signal.\n\n---\n\nSection 4 done. That's the full design. Before I write it up as the spec doc, anything to reshape — especially around chunking (4 chunks vs more/fewer), the deferred-per-agent HeadlessLauncher rollout (start with 3, add rest in follow-ups), or the risks I flagged?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":44,"cache_creation_input_tokens":566,"cache_read_input_tokens":620255,"output_tokens":2445,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":566},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":44,"output_tokens":2445,"cache_read_input_tokens":620255,"cache_creation_input_tokens":566,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":566,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaM2bLNyxGEsFwLYxDpRt","type":"assistant","uuid":"e1662650-006f-4e56-bffe-8e14053472e6","timestamp":"2026-04-23T16:36:36.929Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-review","sessionId":"32ff705a-db92-4346-a9c8-70b631ba581d","version":"2.1.117","gitBranch":"feat/entire-review-multi-agent"}
