{"parentUuid":"775f9e6d-920f-491a-bd67-6dbfd92c8597","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01ABqqr5dMmUjTY5ePgxNjpD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"My mistake — `CalculateTokenUsage` is already implemented for **every** agent in the repo (claudecode, codex, copilotcli, factoryaidroid, geminicli, opencode, external), all satisfying the base `Agent` interface. So token counts are uniformly available.\n\n### Updated token handling in the 2.2 design\n\nEach agent's `CalculateTokenUsage(transcriptData, fromOffset)` method is the source. Flow:\n\n- **At completion** (end of subprocess run): orchestrator reads the agent's transcript file (path resolved via existing agent plumbing — `agent.SessionBaseDirProvider`, etc.), calls `CalculateTokenUsage`, stores the result in the row's `AgentRunResult.TokenUsage`. TUI repaints the row with the final count.\n- **Live updates during the run**: nice-to-have, not needed for 2.2. The preview line gives a sense of progress; the token column can show `—` while running and flip to the final count on completion. Live streaming would require periodic `CalculateTokenUsage` calls against a growing transcript file (polling or fsnotify) — defer to 2.3 if wanted.\n\nThis removes the \"token column empty for codex/gemini\" risk — just drop that bullet from the flagged risks.\n\n### Revised risk list\n\n- ~~Token counting per row~~ — **resolved**, every agent implements `CalculateTokenUsage`, call it on completion.\n- `teatest` dependency — adds `github.com/charmbracelet/x/exp/teatest` as test-only import. Small but explicit in go.mod.\n- Signal handling on Windows — `exec.CommandContext` doesn't send SIGTERM on Windows; accept first-Ctrl+C = SIGKILL on Windows as Phase 2.2 behavior. Note in spec.\n- Parallel API usage — 3 agents hitting the same API provider simultaneously can trigger rate limits. Not our operational concern but add a one-line advisory in the dashboard header.\n\n---\n\nDesign is now tight. Want me to write the spec doc (`docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-22-entire-review-multi-agent-parallel-design.md`) and run the review loop, or anything else to revise first?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":554,"cache_read_input_tokens":625406,"output_tokens":1134,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":554},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1134,"cache_read_input_tokens":625406,"cache_creation_input_tokens":554,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":554,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaM3tZCVmGVfdLc89MmYP","type":"assistant","uuid":"5cfc9e94-71d8-4093-b6ce-da9cf663a5c9","timestamp":"2026-04-23T16:53:13.829Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-review","sessionId":"32ff705a-db92-4346-a9c8-70b631ba581d","version":"2.1.117","gitBranch":"feat/entire-review-multi-agent"}
