{"parentUuid":"dd188795-8443-4f8f-8491-d85d1cced0ca","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01CCbtbZCLrnABnNpZXeaVmq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good question — two separate concerns. Let me unpack.\n\n**Concern 1: Do we still get token usage when running headlessly?**\n\nYes. Running `claude --print` / `codex exec` / `gemini -p` is only a UI-mode difference — no TUI, non-interactive. The subprocess still writes its native transcript file to disk exactly like an interactive session:\n\n- Claude: `~/.claude/projects/<cwd-slug>/<session-id>.jsonl`\n- Codex: `~/.codex/sessions/<timestamp>/<session-id>.jsonl`\n- Gemini: `~/.gemini/tmp/<session-id>/transcript.jsonl`\n- etc. for copilot, opencode, factory-droid\n\nAfter the subprocess exits, we read that file and call the agent's `CalculateTokenUsage(transcriptData, 0)` to get a `*TokenUsage` struct. That's the same transcript the hook-driven session recording uses today, just read at a different time. No data lost by running headless.\n\n**Concern 2: If the user wants to re-open the session in the agent's CLI later?**\n\nSame answer — the transcript file is identical to what an interactive session would produce, so they can pop back into it with the agent's native resume flow:\n\n- `claude --resume <session-id>`\n- `codex resume <session-id>`\n- `gemini` (its own session menu)\n\nThey'll see the full conversation with the agent's own token/cost UI. Nothing about running it headlessly from `entire review` changes the file.\n\n**So the flow for 2.2's TUI token column:**\n\n```\nsubprocess exits →\n  orchestrator resolves transcript path (agent-specific, via SessionBaseDirProvider) →\n  read file from disk →\n  agent.CalculateTokenUsage(data, 0) →\n  row.tokens = result.InputTokens + result.OutputTokens (or however we want to display) →\n  TUI repaints the row with final number\n```\n\nWe never need to parse tokens ourselves — every agent already knows how to do it from its own transcript. We just call the method after the subprocess exits.\n\n**One subtle detail worth flagging**: this only gets us the token count at the END of each agent's run, not live. If you want the TUI to show the token counter ticking up as the agent streams, we'd need to poll `CalculateTokenUsage` every ~second on the growing transcript file. That's cheap but adds complexity — my recommendation is show `—` while running and flip to the final number when done. Live streaming of tokens would be a 2.3-ish polish.\n\nAny of that change how you'd want 2.2 to behave? Or ready for me to write the spec?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1184,"cache_read_input_tokens":625960,"output_tokens":2197,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1184},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":2197,"cache_read_input_tokens":625960,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1184,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1184,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaM4C36kuwqtvHXJPB8me","type":"assistant","uuid":"1e58f4e3-242b-4314-9f75-ead3dcb4bba8","timestamp":"2026-04-23T16:57:23.845Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-review","sessionId":"32ff705a-db92-4346-a9c8-70b631ba581d","version":"2.1.117","gitBranch":"feat/entire-review-multi-agent"}
