{"parentUuid":"9cfe8760-290d-4750-a09f-5133661c53a0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Di7RfV4RGwRbu7FTfxL9VM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01V8iuo5yUKJoA2aQJYqGsG6","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-review/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-22-entire-review-multi-agent-parallel-design.md","content":"# `entire review` — Multi-Agent Parallel Spawn (Sub-phase 2.2)\n\n**Status:** design — awaiting implementation plan\n**Date:** 2026-04-22\n**Author:** Peyton Montei (with Claude Opus 4.7)\n**Base branch:** `feat/entire-review` (PR #993) at tip `874f9a4ba` — includes Phase 1 picker-install + Sub-phase 2.1 spawn-time agent picker + Soph's three picker fixes (external agents, preselection, agent header).\n\n> **Note on repo state:** Phase 1's speculative abstractions (skilldiscovery package, SkillDiscoverer interface, stubs, install hints, runtime verification guard, empty-state notes) have been parked on a local `feat/entire-review-simplify` branch (commit `2d590f7e1`, unpushed) pending coordination with concurrent picker work. This spec assumes the **current** `feat/entire-review` shape — with `skilldiscovery` still in place and install hints still present. The simplification, if it lands separately, doesn't conflict with anything 2.2 introduces.\n\n## Problem\n\nToday `entire review` runs one agent per invocation. When a user has both claude-code and codex configured (per Phase 1 + 2.1), the 2.1 picker asks *which one* to run. Users can't review with **both** simultaneously — they'd have to run `entire review` twice, wait for each TTY session to finish, and manually read both outputs.\n\nUsers who want multi-perspective review — e.g., \"let Claude find style issues while Codex looks for bugs while Gemini scans perf\" — are forced into serial runs that scale poorly and have no unified presentation.\n\n## Goals\n\n1. User can select 2+ configured agents to run the same review in **parallel**.\n2. Each selected agent runs **headlessly** (non-interactive flag: `claude --print`, `codex exec`, `gemini -p`, etc.).\n3. `entire` owns a **bubbletea status-table TUI** showing one row per agent: status (queued / running / done / failed), duration counter, final token usage, one-line preview of latest stdout.\n4. Per-agent failure is independent — a codex crash doesn't kill claude's in-flight run.\n5. Ctrl+C cascades: first press sends SIGTERM to all subprocesses with a 5s grace window; second press within the window escalates to SIGKILL.\n6. On completion, the TUI exits and each agent's **full, uncompacted final response** is dumped sequentially with per-agent headers, followed by a summary line and transcript paths.\n7. Multi-agent runs produce **one multi-session checkpoint** on the next `git commit`, using PR #993's existing multi-session checkpoint infrastructure (numbered subfolders, shared summary).\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- **Ctrl+O live drill-in during the run** — Sub-phase 2.3.\n- **Aggregated / cross-agent summary view** — Sub-phase 2.3.\n- **AI-synthesized cross-agent verdict** — Sub-phase 2.4.\n- **Live token counter ticking during the run** — 2.2 only updates token columns at subprocess completion; polling the growing transcript is 2.3-grade polish.\n- **Streaming stdout scrollback beyond one truncated preview line** — 2.3 adds the full inline view.\n- **Retry of failed agents** — user re-runs manually.\n- **Persisting the multi-agent selection across runs** — every run re-prompts unless `--agent NAME` or (new) `--all` is passed.\n- **Windows graceful shutdown** — `exec.CommandContext` doesn't emit SIGTERM on Windows; accept first-Ctrl+C = SIGKILL there as 2.2 behavior.\n\n## Architecture overview\n\n### Component layout\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  entire review                                                │\n│                                                               │\n│  ┌──────────────┐     ┌──────────────────────────────────┐   │\n│  │ Multi-select │ ──► │ computeEligibleForHeadless(ctx)  │   │\n│  │   picker     │     │ (configured ∩ hooks ∩             │   │\n│  │              │     │  implements HeadlessLauncher)     │   │\n│  └──────────────┘     └──────────────────────────────────┘   │\n│         │                                                     │\n│         ▼                                                     │\n│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐    │\n│  │ multiReviewOrchestrator.Run(ctx, tasks)             │    │\n│  │ ───────────────────────────────                     │    │\n│  │ • Writes shared marker (AgentNames []string)        │    │\n│  │ • Spawns N goroutines, one per task                 │    │\n│  │ • Owns tea.Program for the status TUI               │    │\n│  │ • defer ClearPendingReviewMarker(ctx)               │    │\n│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘    │\n│      │                            │                          │\n│      ▼                            ▼                          │\n│  ┌──────────┐   state msgs   ┌──────────────┐                │\n│  │ per-     │ ◄────────────► │ reviewTUIModel│                │\n│  │ agent    │ preview msgs   │ (bubbletea   │                │\n│  │ runners  │                │  tea.Model)  │                │\n│  │ (N)      │                │              │                │\n│  └──────────┘                └──────────────┘                │\n│      │                                                        │\n│      ▼ (all terminal)                                         │\n│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐    │\n│  │ TUI exits → read transcript → CalculateTokenUsage  │    │\n│  │  → dump per-agent final responses → summary + paths │    │\n│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘    │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n         (independently, each agent's hooks fire)\n                        │\n                        ▼\n             ┌──────────────────────────┐\n             │ adoptPendingReviewMarker │\n             │ Into — multi-agent path  │\n             │                          │\n             │ Read marker, check own   │\n             │ name in AgentNames,      │\n             │ tag session. DO NOT      │\n             │ clear marker — orchestra-│\n             │ tor owns cleanup.        │\n             └──────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Happy-path data flow\n\n1. User runs `entire review` with 2+ configured + hooks-installed + `HeadlessLauncher`-implementing agents.\n2. Phase 1/2.1 eligibility runs first; if the eligible set has ≥2 agents and no `--agent` flag and no `--all` flag, the new multi-select picker fires.\n3. Picker returns selected names (length ≥ 1).\n4. If length == 1 → drop into 2.1's single-agent TTY path (no orchestrator, no TUI).\n5. If length ≥ 2 → `runMultiAgent(ctx, selected)` takes over:\n   - Writes shared marker with `AgentNames: selected`.\n   - Spawns N goroutines, each calling `task.Agent.LaunchHeadlessCmd(ctx, task.Prompt)`.\n   - Each goroutine pipes stdout through a `teeWriter` into (a) a per-agent buffer for later dump and (b) a rate-limited channel that emits preview messages to the TUI.\n   - bubbletea `tea.Program` runs synchronously on the main goroutine; agent goroutines post messages via `tea.Program.Send`.\n6. Independently, each agent subprocess's `UserPromptSubmit` hook fires, reads the shared marker, sees its own name in `AgentNames`, tags its session state with `Kind=agent_review` + recorded prompt/skills. Marker is NOT cleared by hooks.\n7. When all N goroutines finish (terminal status: Done / Failed / Cancelled), TUI receives an \"all done\" signal and `tea.Quit`s.\n8. Orchestrator:\n   - Resolves each transcript path via existing agent plumbing.\n   - Calls `agent.CalculateTokenUsage(transcriptData, 0)` per agent → fills token column in final TUI paint.\n   - Dumps per-agent final response buffers with `─────── <agent> review ───────` headers.\n   - Prints summary line + transcript paths.\n   - `defer ClearPendingReviewMarker(ctx)` cleans up the marker.\n9. Later, user runs `git commit`; condensation walks the N tagged sessions and writes one multi-session checkpoint under `entire/checkpoints/v1/<id[:2]>/<id[2:]>/` with N numbered subfolders — existing PR #993 infrastructure, no changes needed.\n\n### Unit boundaries\n\nSix independent units, each testable on its own:\n\n| Unit | Responsibility | File |\n|---|---|---|\n| `HeadlessLauncher` capability interface | Contract for headless subprocess spawn | `cmd/entire/cli/agent/agent.go` (extension) |\n| Per-agent `HeadlessLauncher` impls | Agent-specific flags (`--print`, `exec`, `-p`, etc.) | `cmd/entire/cli/agent/{claudecode,codex,geminicli,cursor,copilotcli}/headless.go` |\n| Multi-select picker | `promptForAgents(ctx, eligible) ([]string, error)` | `cmd/entire/cli/review.go` |\n| `multiReviewOrchestrator` | Goroutine orchestration, shared marker, SIGTERM/SIGKILL cascade | `cmd/entire/cli/review_multi.go` (new) |\n| `reviewTUIModel` | bubbletea model for status table; pure rendering | `cmd/entire/cli/review_tui.go` (new) |\n| Hook adoption — multi-agent path | `adoptPendingReviewMarkerInto` honors `AgentNames` | `cmd/entire/cli/review.go` (extension) |\n\n## Data model\n\n### `HeadlessLauncher` capability interface\n\nNew optional interface alongside the existing `Launcher` (which keeps 2.1's TTY-takeover path):\n\n```go\n// cmd/entire/cli/agent/agent.go — add after Launcher\n\n// HeadlessLauncher is implemented by agents that support running a prompt\n// in non-interactive mode. The subprocess writes its native transcript to\n// disk (same file as an interactive session) and exits when the prompt\n// completes. Used by `entire review`'s multi-agent TUI to spawn N parallel\n// reviews. Agents that implement only Launcher (interactive TTY only)\n// remain reachable via the single-agent spawn path from Sub-phase 2.1.\n//\n// Contract:\n//   - LaunchHeadlessCmd returns an *exec.Cmd with Stdout/Stderr pipes left\n//     for the caller to assign (orchestrator wires them to tees + buffers).\n//   - Stdin is left nil; the prompt is passed as the positional arg or\n//     equivalent per-agent flag.\n//   - UserPromptSubmit hook must fire during the run so the pending-review\n//     marker adoption pipeline works.\n//   - Subprocess must terminate on its own once the prompt completes; the\n//     orchestrator does not send a graceful signal to end the run (only\n//     to cancel it).\ntype HeadlessLauncher interface {\n    Agent\n    LaunchHeadlessCmd(ctx context.Context, initialPrompt string) (*exec.Cmd, error)\n}\n```\n\nPer-agent implementations are thin — each agent already has a `GenerateText` function that invokes itself headlessly for things like compact-transcript summaries. `LaunchHeadlessCmd` returns the `*exec.Cmd` rather than running it.\n\n- **Claude Code**: `claude --print \"<prompt>\"` — existing Phase 1/2.1 plumbing via `exec.LookPath(\"claude\")`.\n- **Codex**: `codex exec \"<prompt>\"`.\n- **Gemini**: `gemini -p \"<prompt>\"` (non-interactive).\n- **Cursor**: `cursor-agent --print --force --trust --workspace <tmpdir>` (as `cursor/generate.go` does today).\n- **Copilot CLI**: `copilot -p \"<prompt>\" --allow-all-tools --silent`.\n- **External agents, opencode, factoryai-droid**: rollout as follow-ups if they support non-interactive modes. Not blocking 2.2 initial ship.\n\n### `PendingReviewMarker` extension\n\nOne new field, backwards-compatible via JSON's tolerance for missing keys:\n\n```go\ntype PendingReviewMarker struct {\n    AgentName    string    `json:\"agent_name,omitempty\"`    // Phase 1 / 2.1 single-agent\n    AgentNames   []string  `json:\"agent_names,omitempty\"`   // NEW — multi-agent list\n    Skills       []string  `json:\"skills\"`                  // unchanged\n    Prompt       string    `json:\"prompt,omitempty\"`        // unchanged\n    StartingSHA  string    `json:\"starting_sha\"`            // unchanged\n    StartedAt    time.Time `json:\"started_at\"`              // unchanged\n    WorktreePath string    `json:\"worktree_path,omitempty\"` // unchanged\n}\n```\n\n### Hook adoption (`adoptPendingReviewMarkerInto`) — multi-agent branch\n\n```\nread marker\nif marker.AgentName != \"\":                    # Phase 1/2.1 path, unchanged\n    (existing logic — adopt if own name matches, clear marker)\nelif len(marker.AgentNames) > 0:              # NEW — multi-agent\n    if agentName not in AgentNames: leave alone\n    else: tag session with Kind=agent_review + Prompt + Skills\n          # DO NOT clear marker — orchestrator owns cleanup\nelse:\n    leave alone  (no adoption criteria)\n```\n\nRationale for hooks not clearing: simpler hook code, no concurrent-write-to-shared-marker problem, orchestrator already has a clear lifecycle. If orchestrator crashes before cleanup, marker self-heals on next run via the existing stale-marker handling.\n\n### New types (orchestrator home)\n\nAll in `cmd/entire/cli/review_multi.go`:\n\n```go\ntype MultiAgentTask struct {\n    Agent          agent.HeadlessLauncher\n    Name           string          // registry key, also used for marker match\n    Prompt         string          // from composeReviewPrompt(cfg)\n}\n\ntype AgentRunStatus int\nconst (\n    AgentRunQueued AgentRunStatus = iota\n    AgentRunRunning\n    AgentRunDone\n    AgentRunFailed\n    AgentRunCancelled\n)\n\ntype AgentRunResult struct {\n    Name           string\n    Status         AgentRunStatus\n    ExitCode       int               // 0 if Done\n    Duration       time.Duration\n    FinalOutput    []byte            // full stdout for completion dump\n    Err            error             // non-nil for Failed / Cancelled\n    TokenUsage     *agent.TokenUsage // populated post-exit via CalculateTokenUsage\n    TranscriptPath string            // resolved post-exit; empty if session never tagged\n}\n\ntype MultiRunResult struct {\n    Runs       []AgentRunResult  // one per input task, ordered by tasks slice\n    Duration   time.Duration     // wall-clock for the whole run\n    Cancelled  bool              // user Ctrl+C during run\n}\n```\n\n### `runReviewDeps` extensions\n\n```go\ntype runReviewDeps struct {\n    promptForAgentFn   func(ctx, []agentChoice) (string, error)                          // existing (2.1)\n    promptForAgentsFn  func(ctx, []agentChoice) ([]string, error)                        // NEW\n    runMultiAgentFn    func(ctx, []MultiAgentTask, io.Writer) (MultiRunResult, error)    // NEW — full orchestrator entry\n}\n```\n\nTests stub `runMultiAgentFn` with a deterministic fake that records invocations — no real subprocesses, no real bubbletea. Production wiring (nil → real function) kicks in as before.\n\n## Runtime orchestration\n\n### `multiReviewOrchestrator.Run` lifecycle\n\n```\nRun(ctx, tasks, out) (MultiRunResult, error):\n\n  1. Write shared marker with AgentNames = [t.Name for t in tasks].\n     defer ClearPendingReviewMarker(ctx)\n\n  2. Build per-task channels + stdout buffers.\n\n  3. program := tea.NewProgram(initialTUIModel(tasks), tea.WithAltScreen())\n\n  4. For each task: start goroutine\n       cmd, err := task.Agent.LaunchHeadlessCmd(ctx, task.Prompt)\n       if err != nil: post AgentRunMsg{Name, Failed, Err}; return\n       cmd.Stdout = teeWriter(&buf, previewChan)\n       cmd.Stderr = teeWriter(&buf, previewChan)\n       post AgentRunMsg{Name, Running, startTime=now()}\n       err = cmd.Run()\n       duration = now() - startTime\n       post AgentRunMsg{Name, terminalStatus(err), duration, FinalOutput: buf, Err: err}\n\n  5. Goroutine #2 watches previewChan → posts agentPreviewMsg to the Program.\n\n  6. program.Run() blocks until Model quits.\n\n  7. Resolve TranscriptPath + TokenUsage per completed task (post-exit reads).\n\n  8. Print per-agent dumps + summary + transcript paths to out.\n\n  9. Return MultiRunResult{Runs, Duration, Cancelled}.\n```\n\n### Cancellation (Ctrl+C cascade)\n\n- `ctx` passed from the cobra command is cancellation-aware.\n- First Ctrl+C → Go's default signal handler cancels ctx → `exec.CommandContext`-spawned subprocesses receive SIGTERM automatically (on Unix) or are killed immediately (on Windows).\n- TUI model receives cancellation signal via a `cancelMsg` posted from a small signal-watcher goroutine that the orchestrator spawns; flips running rows to `⊘ cancelling…`.\n- Watchdog: if any subprocess hasn't exited 5s after SIGTERM, send SIGKILL.\n- Second Ctrl+C within the window → immediate SIGKILL bypass of the 5s grace.\n- `MultiRunResult.Cancelled = true` so the summary line reflects the cancel path.\n\n### bubbletea `reviewTUIModel`\n\n```go\n// cmd/entire/cli/review_tui.go — new file\n\ntype reviewTUIModel struct {\n    tasks      []MultiAgentTask\n    rows       []rowState               // index-aligned with tasks\n    spinner    spinner.Model            // shared across all running rows\n    startTime  time.Time\n    allDone    bool\n    cancelling bool\n}\n\ntype rowState struct {\n    name     string\n    status   AgentRunStatus\n    duration time.Duration            // set at exit; \"now() - startTime\" for running\n    tokens   int                      // 0 while running; final post-exit\n    preview  string                   // last truncated line of stdout\n    exitCode int\n}\n\n// Messages consumed:\ntype agentStateMsg struct { name string; status AgentRunStatus; duration time.Duration; exitCode int; tokens int }\ntype agentPreviewMsg struct { name string; line string }    // already ANSI-stripped + width-truncated\ntype cancelMsg struct{}\ntype tickMsg time.Time\n```\n\n`View()` renders the table + bottom \"N of M complete\" counter. `Update` handles the three message types plus ticks for spinner + duration. When `allDone` becomes true OR `cancelling` → 0 running rows, Update returns `tea.Quit`.\n\nPreview messages are rate-limited to max ~10/sec per row in the teeWriter — chatty agents can't starve the TUI event loop.\n\n### Completion output\n\nAfter `program.Run()` returns and token usage is resolved:\n\n```\nfor i, task := range tasks:\n    result := runs[i]\n    fmt.Fprintf(out, \"\\n─────── %s review ───────\\n\", task.Name)\n    if result.Status == Failed:\n        fmt.Fprintf(out, \"(failed — exit %d)\\n\", result.ExitCode)\n        if result.Err != nil:\n            fmt.Fprintf(out, \"%v\\n\\n\", result.Err)\n    else if result.Status == Cancelled:\n        fmt.Fprintln(out, \"(cancelled)\\n\")\n    out.Write(result.FinalOutput)   // full uncompacted final response\n\n// Summary line\nfmt.Fprintln(out)\nfmt.Fprintf(out, \"✓ %d agents done in %s (%d succeeded, %d failed, %d cancelled)\\n\",\n    len(tasks), totalDuration, nSucceeded, nFailed, nCancelled)\nfmt.Fprintln(out, \"  Run `git commit` to attach the review to the next checkpoint.\")\n\n// Transcript paths (any agent whose session got tagged)\nfmt.Fprintln(out, \"\\n  Full transcripts (including tool calls + reasoning):\")\nfor _, run := range runs:\n    if run.TranscriptPath == \"\":\n        continue\n    fmt.Fprintf(out, \"    %-12s → %s\\n\", run.Name, run.TranscriptPath)\n```\n\n## Picker flow\n\nExtending 2.1's eligibility check + picker:\n\n```\neligible := computeEligibleConfigured(ctx, s)                  // 2.1's existing helper\nif len(eligible) == 0:\n    # existing \"hooks not installed\" error path\nelif agentOverride != \"\":                                       # --agent NAME\n    # single-agent path (existing 2.1)\nelif flagAllEligible:                                           # NEW --all flag\n    selected = eligible (filtered to those implementing HeadlessLauncher)\n    route to runMultiAgent\nelif len(eligible) == 1:\n    # single-agent fast path (existing)\nelse:                                                           # len > 1, interactive\n    # NEW: filter eligible further to HeadlessLauncher-implementers\n    runnable := [e for e in eligible if implements HeadlessLauncher]\n    if len(runnable) < 2:\n        # Fall back to 2.1's single-select (some agents configured but\n        # can't run headless in parallel; 2.1 path handles the rest)\n        picked, err = deps.promptForAgentFn(ctx, eligible)\n        agentOverride = picked\n    else:\n        selected, err = deps.promptForAgentsFn(ctx, runnable)\n        if len(selected) == 0: return silent error (user cancel)\n        if len(selected) == 1:\n            agentOverride = selected[0]      # drop into single-agent path\n        else:\n            # multi-agent route\n            result, err = deps.runMultiAgentFn(ctx, tasks, out)\n            return\n```\n\n### `promptForAgents`\n\n```go\nfunc promptForAgents(ctx context.Context, eligible []agentChoice) ([]string, error)\n```\n\n`huh.NewMultiSelect[string]()` wrapped with `NewAccessibleForm`. No pre-checked options — user actively picks. Ctrl+C returns `[]` + `context.Canceled`. Empty selection = user cancel.\n\n## Testing strategy\n\n### Unit — `cli/review_test.go` extensions\n\n- `TestPromptForAgents_EmptySelectionCancels` — stub returns `[]`, runReview exits with silent error, no marker.\n- `TestMultiReview_PreservesSingleAgentPath` — picker returns 1 name → existing single-agent path runs, `runMultiAgentFn` never called.\n- `TestMultiReview_OrchestratorReceivesTasks` — picker returns ≥2 names → stubbed `runMultiAgentFn` receives the correct `[]MultiAgentTask` (ordering, names, prompts).\n\n### Unit — new `cli/review_multi_test.go`\n\nWith a fake `HeadlessLauncher` that returns a controllable `*exec.Cmd`:\n\n- `TestOrchestrator_WritesSharedMarker` — assert marker has `AgentNames: [...]` after Run starts.\n- `TestOrchestrator_ClearsMarkerOnHappyExit` — fake agents exit cleanly → marker absent after Run returns.\n- `TestOrchestrator_ClearsMarkerOnCancel` — cancel ctx → subprocesses receive cancellation → marker absent.\n- `TestOrchestrator_FailurePerAgentIndependent` — fake agent A fails, B + C succeed → `MultiRunResult.Runs` has mixed statuses.\n- `TestOrchestrator_ResolvesTokenUsagePostExit` — fake agent writes a fake transcript → `CalculateTokenUsage` called → `AgentRunResult.TokenUsage` populated.\n\n### Unit — new `cli/review_tui_test.go`\n\nUsing `github.com/charmbracelet/x/exp/teatest` for headless bubbletea testing:\n\n- `TestTUIModel_InitialViewAllQueued`.\n- `TestTUIModel_TransitionsToRunningOnMsg`.\n- `TestTUIModel_DoneFlipsQuits` — all-done messages produce `tea.Quit`.\n- `TestTUIModel_PreviewTruncates` — preview msg with 200-char line → row preview ≤ terminal-width.\n- `TestTUIModel_CancelShowsOverlay` — `cancelMsg` flips running rows to cancelling state.\n\n### Unit — hook adoption — `cli/lifecycle_test.go` extensions\n\n- `TestAdoptMarker_MultiAgent_AgentInListAdopts` — marker `AgentNames: [A, B]`, session for A → adopts + tags.\n- `TestAdoptMarker_MultiAgent_AgentNotInListIgnores` — marker `AgentNames: [A, B]`, session for C → no adopt, marker unchanged.\n- `TestAdoptMarker_MultiAgent_DoesNotClearMarker` — A adopts, marker still present on disk (orchestrator owns cleanup).\n- `TestAdoptMarker_SingleAgent_UnchangedBehavior` — existing `AgentName:` field path still clears on adopt.\n\n### No E2E additions\n\nExisting Vogon canary continues to cover spawn → adopt → commit. Multi-agent E2E requires 2+ real agents in parallel — expensive and fragile. Defer until the feature ships and real usage surfaces a regression we can reproduce deterministically.\n\n## Chunking + commit plan\n\n**Four chunks, one commit each** — on branch `feat/entire-review-multi-agent`:\n\n| # | Chunk | Approx LOC | Files new/modified |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `HeadlessLauncher` interface + 3-5 per-agent impls | +250 / -0 | agent.go, claudecode/headless.go, codex/headless.go, geminicli/headless.go, plus tests |\n| 2 | Multi-select picker (`promptForAgents`) + `runReviewDeps` extensions + dispatch logic in `runReview` | +200 / -20 | review.go, review_test.go |\n| 3 | `multiReviewOrchestrator` + `PendingReviewMarker.AgentNames` + hook adoption multi-agent branch | +350 / -10 | review_multi.go (new), review.go, lifecycle_test.go |\n| 4 | `reviewTUIModel` + bubbletea wiring + preview plumbing + completion dump | +400 / -0 | review_tui.go (new), review_multi.go |\n\nEach chunk ends with `mise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run check && mise run dup`; green is the gate for commit.\n\n## Risks\n\n- **`teatest` dependency.** Adding `github.com/charmbracelet/x/exp/teatest` as test import. Small but explicit in go.mod.\n- **Parallel API rate limits.** Three agents hitting the same API provider simultaneously can trigger 429s. Not our operational concern but we can surface a one-line advisory in the dashboard header (\"running N parallel reviews — API rate limits apply\").\n- **Windows graceful shutdown.** Covered in Non-goals. First-Ctrl+C behavior on Windows is SIGKILL via `exec.CommandContext`.\n- **Stale markers on orchestrator crash.** Mitigated by Phase 1's existing stale-marker sweep. If orchestrator dies mid-run and the marker persists, next `entire review` run (single or multi) clears it per existing worktree-scoping logic.\n\n## Follow-ups (explicit, for 2.3 / 2.4)\n\n- **Sub-phase 2.3:** Ctrl+O live drill-in (open a scrollable full-screen transcript pane for one agent while others keep running); aggregated mechanical cross-agent summary (\"consensus findings\" / \"divergent findings\" sections) without AI synthesis.\n- **Sub-phase 2.4:** AI-synthesized cross-agent verdict — call one more agent (user-configurable synthesizer) to read all N outputs and produce a meta-review. Optional flag; doesn't change 2.2/2.3 default behavior.\n- **Live token counter ticks** — polling `CalculateTokenUsage` on the growing transcript during the run (2.3 polish).\n- **Per-agent retry button in the TUI** — if a run fails, offer to re-launch just that agent. Requires some state machine work — 2.3 or later.\n- **Remaining `HeadlessLauncher` implementations** — opencode, factoryai-droid, external agents. Land as needed when users configure them for review.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":629351,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":10685,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":629351,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":10685,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":629351,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":629351},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaM6ky8npEsWbiPKXr6ja","type":"assistant","uuid":"93beb070-6d99-4138-9865-4aedb9ab433e","timestamp":"2026-04-23T17:33:10.712Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-review","sessionId":"32ff705a-db92-4346-a9c8-70b631ba581d","version":"2.1.117","gitBranch":"feat/entire-review-multi-agent"}
