{"parentUuid":"a22e8833-a09a-4285-b3dc-90d5c72f5617","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Cx4LxTPdMP1uMJjfi7HQqF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm using the writing-plans skill to create the implementation plan."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6553,"cache_read_input_tokens":649668,"output_tokens":31806,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6553,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":31806,"cache_read_input_tokens":649668,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6553,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6553},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaM8ZMkUT2ZHAmKHMdme6","type":"assistant","uuid":"57aa185b-0add-4f16-a85e-45a5a5b32edb","timestamp":"2026-04-23T17:54:19.961Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-review","sessionId":"32ff705a-db92-4346-a9c8-70b631ba581d","version":"2.1.117","gitBranch":"feat/entire-review-multi-agent"}
{"parentUuid":"57aa185b-0add-4f16-a85e-45a5a5b32edb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Cx4LxTPdMP1uMJjfi7HQqF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011LttGqDU5ymjmWvWQk8VeN","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-review/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-04-22-entire-review-multi-agent-parallel.md","content":"# `entire review` Multi-Agent Parallel Spawn — Implementation Plan\n\n> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (if subagents available) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.\n\n**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-22-entire-review-multi-agent-parallel-design.md`\n\n**Goal:** `entire review` can run 2+ configured agents in parallel via a new `HeadlessLauncher` capability interface, showing live status in a bubbletea TUI and dumping each agent's full final response on completion.\n\n**Architecture:** New optional `HeadlessLauncher` capability interface alongside the existing `Launcher`; per-agent implementations wrap their existing non-interactive CLI flags. A new `multiReviewOrchestrator` spawns goroutines, owns a shared `PendingReviewMarker` with `AgentNames []string`, and wires subprocess stdout into a bubbletea `reviewTUIModel`. Hook adoption gains a multi-agent branch that preserves Phase 1/2.1 worktree + SHA guards. Completion dumps each agent's full final response sequentially with transcript paths.\n\n**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26.x, Cobra, huh, bubbletea (`charmbracelet/bubbletea`), bubbletea test harness (`charmbracelet/x/exp/teatest`), `mise`/`golangci-lint`/Vogon canary for CI.\n\n**Branch strategy:** Four commits directly on `feat/entire-review-multi-agent` (tracking `origin/feat/entire-review` at tip `874f9a4ba`). No new branch per chunk.\n\n**Chunk order is strict** — each chunk type-checks against the previous:\n\n1. `HeadlessLauncher` interface + per-agent impls\n2. Multi-select picker + dispatch (type-checks `HeadlessLauncher`)\n3. Orchestrator + shared marker + hook adoption (uses Chunk 2's dispatch entry point)\n4. bubbletea TUI Model (consumes Chunk 3's message types)\n\n---\n\n## Preamble — confirm base branch state\n\n- [ ] **P.1: Verify working branch**\n\nRun: `git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD`\nExpected: `feat/entire-review-multi-agent`. Stop if anything else.\n\n- [ ] **P.2: Verify Phase 1 + 2.1 state present**\n\nRun:\n```bash\ngrep -n \"func selectReviewAgent\\|func verifyConfiguredSkillsInstalled\\|func confirmFirstRunSetup\\|func promptForAgent\\|func splitSavedPicks\" cmd/entire/cli/review.go\ngrep -n \"type PendingReviewMarker\\|func adoptPendingReviewMarkerInto\" cmd/entire/cli/review.go\n```\nExpected: all symbols present. Stop if any missing — the branch is wrong.\n\n- [ ] **P.3: Check bubbletea is already a dependency**\n\nRun: `grep charmbracelet/bubbletea go.mod`\nExpected: match. huh is built on bubbletea so the base library is already there. If missing, surface to user — `bubbletea` is required for Chunk 4.\n\n- [ ] **P.4: Baseline `mise run check`**\n\nRun: `mise run check`\nExpected: PASS. Baselines the tree.\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 1 — `HeadlessLauncher` capability interface + per-agent implementations\n\nOne commit at the end. Lands the contract plus three real implementations. Cursor + Copilot CLI + opencode + factoryai-droid + external follow in later commits per the spec's \"Follow-ups\" section.\n\n### Files\n\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/agent.go` — add `HeadlessLauncher` interface near existing `Launcher` (~line 268).\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/headless.go` — Claude Code implementation.\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/headless_test.go`.\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/headless.go` — Codex implementation.\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/headless_test.go`.\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/headless.go` — Gemini CLI implementation.\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/headless_test.go`.\n\n### Task 1.1 — Add `HeadlessLauncher` capability interface\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Verify symbol absent**\n\nRun: `grep -n \"HeadlessLauncher\" cmd/entire/cli/agent/agent.go`\nExpected: zero matches.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Add interface definition**\n\nInsert into `cmd/entire/cli/agent/agent.go` immediately after the existing `Launcher` interface (search for `type Launcher interface`; add the new type after its closing brace):\n\n```go\n// HeadlessLauncher is implemented by agents that support running a prompt\n// in non-interactive mode. The subprocess writes its native transcript to\n// disk (same file as an interactive session) and exits when the prompt\n// completes. Used by `entire review`'s multi-agent TUI to spawn N parallel\n// reviews; agents that implement only Launcher (interactive TTY only)\n// remain reachable via the single-agent spawn path from Sub-phase 2.1.\n//\n// Contract:\n//   - LaunchHeadlessCmd returns an *exec.Cmd with Stdout/Stderr pipes left\n//     for the caller to assign (orchestrator wires them to tees + buffers).\n//   - Stdin is left nil; the prompt is passed as the positional arg or\n//     equivalent per-agent flag.\n//   - UserPromptSubmit hook must fire during the run so the pending-review\n//     marker adoption pipeline works.\n//   - Subprocess must terminate on its own once the prompt completes. The\n//     orchestrator does not send a graceful signal to end the run — only\n//     to cancel it (SIGTERM via ctx cancel).\ntype HeadlessLauncher interface {\n\tAgent\n\tLaunchHeadlessCmd(ctx context.Context, initialPrompt string) (*exec.Cmd, error)\n}\n```\n\n`context` and `os/exec` are already imported at the top of the file — no new imports needed.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Verify package compiles**\n\nRun: `go build ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/...`\nExpected: PASS.\n\n### Task 1.2 — Claude Code `LaunchHeadlessCmd`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Writ